"locale":"zh-CN"},"579":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"检测不到 Shell","locale":"zh-CN"},"580":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"显式传 `--shell powershell/bash/zsh/cmd`；不要靠修改 `$SHELL` 或 COMSPEC","locale":"zh-CN"},"581":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Windows Zsh 报 `D:\\…` command not found","locale":"zh-CN"},"582":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"直接运行新 EXE，检查 `cygpath`，重新加载 env / 更新 shell init","locale":"zh-CN"},"583":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"PowerShell 加载了错误 profile","locale":"zh-CN"},"584":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"明确 `--shell-executable pwsh` 或 `powershell.exe`，也可用 `--profile`","locale":"zh-CN"},"585":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"版本前缀匹配多个组合","locale":"zh-CN"},"586":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"`list --json` 查看候选，使用完整托管目录键 或固定别名","locale":"zh-CN"},"587":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"无法把实际版本映射到下载 ID","locale":"zh-CN"},"588":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"`list-remote` 查询后显式指定 `--toolset-id` / `--sdk-id`，保留项目约束","locale":"zh-CN"},"589":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"最近项目文件损坏","locale":"zh-CN"},"590":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"修正该文件；不会自动跳过它使用父级或 default","locale":"zh-CN"},"591":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"下载失败","locale":"zh-CN"},"592":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"检查错误中 URL、代理、网络；区分完整缓存与下载工作区","locale":"zh-CN"},"593":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"删除文件后无法使用","locale":"zh-CN"},"594":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"托管目录缺失或必要文件不全时重新 install；其他损坏加 `--reinstall`","locale":"zh-CN"},"595":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"安装中断留下 .stage / .old","locale":"zh-CN"},"596":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"重新执行同一安装；安装会清理暂存树，必要时还原旧树后重试","locale":"zh-CN"},"597":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"外部目录移动后路径失效","locale":"zh-CN"},"598":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"`import --dir NEW --name NAME` 更新原引用","locale":"zh-CN"},"599":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"单个引用文件损坏","locale":"zh-CN"},"600":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"修正或 `remove NAME` 删除该引用；其他目录继续可用","locale":"zh-CN"},"601":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"外部工具链未出现在列表","locale":"zh-CN"},"602":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"用 `import --dir PATH --name NAME` 引用已有目录","locale":"zh-CN"},"603":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"更新缺少资产或 digest","locale":"zh-CN"},"604":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"检查 Release 是否包含与程序架构匹配的 EXE 和 SHA-256 digest","locale":"zh-CN"},"605":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Windows 自删失败","locale":"zh-CN"},"606":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"查看显示目录的 failure.txt，关闭占用进程后重新运行 uninstall.ps1","locale":"zh-CN"},"607":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"优先保留完整错误、命令、Shell 类型与 `hanamori --version`。运行 `config show --resolved` 可以查看配置来源；`doctor --json` 只诊断不修复，有错误时仍返回非零状态。分享日志前注意其中可能包含完整请求 URL。","locale":"zh-CN"},"608":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"导入目录不能用 `uninstall` 删除，使用 `remove` 取消引用。锁文件存在不代表还被占用；不要手工删除锁来绕过占用错误。先前已完成的卸载不会因后续失败自动回滚。`doctor` 只做布局和必要文件检查，不验证每个已安装文件的哈希。","locale":"zh-CN"},"609":{"id":"/docs/upgrade","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","type":"page","content":"自我更新","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori 文档","维护与参考"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/upgrade","locale":"zh-CN"},"610":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-0","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"从 GitHub Release 验证并替换当前 Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC 程序。","locale":"zh-CN"},"611":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-1","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"仅 Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC 构建支持。`--check` 查询版本和程序路径，不下载 EXE、不写文件；`--force` 允许重装相同版本，不能与 `--check` 合用。任何模式都不降级较新构建、不选择 prerelease、不跳过验证。","locale":"zh-CN"},"612":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-2","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"更新器精确下载最新稳定 Release 中与当前程序架构匹配的 EXE。资产必须有 SHA-256 digest，哈希与大小必须匹配，候选程序必须在十秒内通过 `hanamori --version` 报告预期版本。缺少新版资产或验证失败时不替换旧程序。","locale":"zh-CN"},"613":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-3","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"代理采用 `--proxy`、`HANAMORI_PROXY` 或配置文件的 proxy。可选 `GITHUB_TOKEN` 仅用于 API 查询，不发送给资产下载请求；它不意味着私有资产下载必然可用。工具链 mirror、cache、download-dir 和项目文件不控制更新。","locale":"zh-CN"},"614":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-4","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"更新需要程序目录写权限。同目录创建暂存与 `<executable>.update.lock`，旧程序重命名为 `<executable>.outdated`，在下一次实际更新时尝试删除。新程序通过验证后，若删除备份被占用阻止，Windows Restart Manager 会关闭使用备份的进程并重试；无法释放时按错误提示手动处理。锁文件可能留下，不要删除它来绕过正在进行的操作。","locale":"zh-CN"},"615":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-5","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"两次 rename 不是原子事务。替换失败尝试恢复原程序；若进程被终止在两次重命名之间，且原程序名已不存在，将 `.outdated` 改回原名再重试。回滚失败会显示具体路径。更新不修改工具链、引用或 Shell 配置；已有旧钩子需要时按Shell 文档重新生成。","locale":"zh-CN"},"616":{"id":"/docs/upgrade-6","page_id":"/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/upgrade","content":"自我更新保持当前程序的架构：x64 程序选择 x64 资产，ARM64 程序选择 `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe`，不会按操作系统架构切换程序。","locale":"zh-CN"},"617":{"id":"/docs/website","page_id":"/docs/website","type":"page","content":"网站维护","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori 文档","开发"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/website","locale":"zh-CN"},"618":{"id":"/docs/website-0","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website","content":"维护首页、下载页、中英文档和静态部署。","locale":"zh-CN"},"619":{"id":"/docs/website-1","page_id":"/docs/website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"内容与配置","locale":"zh-CN"},"620":{"id":"/docs/website-2","page_id":"/docs/website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/website#构建与发布","content":"构建与发布","locale":"zh-CN"},"621":{"id":"/docs/website-3","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website","content":"网站位于 `site/`，从 RVC Next 的 Fumadocs/TanStack Start 框架适配。使用 React、Tailwind、MDX、Bun 与 Vitest；来源与许可说明见 `site/NOTICE`、`site/LICENSE`。","locale":"zh-CN"},"622":{"id":"/docs/website-4","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website","content":"开发服务器为 `127.0.0.1:3000`，静态产物为 `.output/public`。首次类型检查如尚无路由生成文件，先运行 build 或启动 dev 让路由插件生成；不手工编辑 `src/routeTree.gen.ts`，不提交缓存与构建产物。","locale":"zh-CN"},"623":{"id":"/docs/website-5","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"`content/docs/PAGE.mdx` 是中文，`PAGE.en.mdx` 是英文，frontmatter 包含 title 和 description。","locale":"zh-CN"},"624":{"id":"/docs/website-6","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"两份 `meta.json`/`meta.en.json` 使用同一 slug 顺序。公开文档链接为 `/docs/PAGE`，语言切换在同一地址完成，不另建语言路由。","locale":"zh-CN"},"625":{"id":"/docs/website-7","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"首页文案在 `src/lib/site-copy.ts`，布局与交互组件在 `src/components/`。","locale":"zh-CN"},"626":{"id":"/docs/website-8","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"`src/lib/releases.ts` 只接受指定名称的稳定 Release 资产；查询失败与没有匹配资产分开展示。","locale":"zh-CN"},"627":{"id":"/docs/website-9","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"MDX 正文中的尖括号、花括号需要转义或放入代码块，不能直接当普通 Markdown 使用。","locale":"zh-CN"},"628":{"id":"/docs/website-10","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#内容与配置","content":"Umami 统计脚本及网站 ID 配置位于 `src/routes/__root.tsx`。文档评论使用 Hanamori GitHub Discussions 的 `Comment` 分类，配置位于 `src/lib/giscus.ts`。Giscus 按 pathname 关联讨论，使用中文（`zh-CN`）界面，并跟随系统配色，无需额外设置评论相关环境变量。","locale":"zh-CN"},"629":{"id":"/docs/website-11","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#构建与发布","content":"当前固定版本的静态 Server Function 中间件会把缓存请求指向根路径；`vite.config.ts` 的构建转换为客户端请求补上 base path，缓存文件仍输出到产物根目录。升级这项依赖时，必须重新检查子路径下的文档导航。","locale":"zh-CN"},"630":{"id":"/docs/website-12","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#构建与发布","content":"自定义域名或根路径部署使用默认 `/`。静态整理脚本验证首页、下载页、文档和搜索产物，并生成 404 回退。新增顶层页面时同步预渲染配置和检查列表。","locale":"zh-CN"},"631":{"id":"/docs/website-13","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#构建与发布","content":"GitHub Actions 的 site workflow 在 PR 中验证构建；main 分支的网站变更或在 main 上手动运行工作流时，验证通过后使用仓库密钥 `GITEE_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY` 将 `.output/public` 强制推送到 `gh-pages` 分支。密钥需要具有仓库写入权限，仓库 Pages 的 Source 选择 `Deploy from a branch`，分支选择 `gh-pages`，目录选择 `/ (root)`。Netlify、Cloudflare Pages 和 Vercel 的配置同样使用 `.output/public`，需要各平台分别配置项目。","locale":"zh-CN"},"632":{"id":"/docs/website-14","page_id":"/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/website#构建与发布","content":"验证根路径与 `/Hanamori/`：深层链接刷新、两种语言、搜索结果跳转、主题、移动布局、减少动画偏好，以及无公开 Release/网络失败/有匹配资产的下载状态。不要把 Node 开发服务器可用当成静态部署已经可用。","locale":"zh-CN"},"633":{"id":"/en/docs/aliases","page_id":"/en/docs/aliases","type":"page","content":"Aliases and defaults","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Toolchains and execution"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/aliases","locale":"en"},"634":{"id":"/en/docs/aliases-0","page_id":"/en/docs/aliases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/aliases","content":"Name fixed installations rather than chaining mutable aliases.","locale":"en"},"635":{"id":"/en/docs/aliases-1","page_id":"/en/docs/aliases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/aliases","content":"References are separate JSON files under `<manager>/references/`. Managed references contain a directory key; external references contain a path and selected actual versions. They never claim files are installed.","locale":"en"},"636":{"id":"/en/docs/aliases-2","page_id":"/en/docs/aliases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/aliases","content":"`alias SELECTOR NAME` accepts a managed key, reference, external `@name` key or unique actual-version prefix. It creates or updates a name. `default stable` copies stable's target: redirecting stable later does not change default or an active session.","locale":"en"},"637":{"id":"/en/docs/aliases-3","page_id":"/en/docs/aliases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/aliases","content":"Names contain 1–64 letters, digits, hyphens or underscores, excluding command names. `default` is allowed. Removing a nonexistent name succeeds. `remove NAME` and `unalias NAME` remove only that reference. Uninstalling a managed directory removes its managed references.","locale":"en"},"638":{"id":"/en/docs/aliases-4","page_id":"/en/docs/aliases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/aliases","content":"Deleting a directory leaves references dangling without blocking reinstallation. Reinstalling the same key restores them. One malformed reference does not hide other installations; doctor reports it.","locale":"en"},"639":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture","locale":"en"},"640":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-0","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Workspace responsibilities, directory discovery and references.","locale":"en"},"641":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-1","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/architecture#extraction-and-publication","content":"Extraction and publication","locale":"en"},"642":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-2","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"The environment includes PATH, INCLUDE, LIB, `CC`/`CXX`, `VCToolsVersion`,\n`VCToolsInstallDir`, `VCINSTALLDIR`, `VSCMD_ARG_HOST_ARCH`, `VSCMD_ARG_TGT_ARCH`,\n`DISTUTILS_USE_SDK`, and SDK root/bin/version variables when applicable. POSIX shells get\nPOSIX executable paths; compiler-consumed INCLUDE/LIB paths retain Windows form. Hanamori\ndoes not generate `vcvarsall.bat` or `vcvars64.bat`.","locale":"en"},"643":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-3","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`src/main.rs` parses and exits; `src/cli/` defines the command tree and each command's\narguments; `src/commands/` runs the commands and prints their output. `src/config.rs`\nresolves typed inputs and retains source diagnostics separately. Everything is one\n`hanamori` crate whose top-level modules form layers that only depend downward:","locale":"en"},"644":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-4","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Layer","locale":"en"},"645":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-5","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Modules","locale":"en"},"646":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-6","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Responsibility","locale":"en"},"647":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-7","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"May use","locale":"en"},"648":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-8","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"foundation","locale":"en"},"649":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-9","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`env`, `msbuild`, `file_usage`, `fs`, `identity`, `locking`, `serde_helpers`, `version`","locale":"en"},"650":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-10","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Paths, locking, file usage handling, layout, versions and identity","locale":"en"},"651":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-11","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"—","locale":"en"},"652":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-12","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"archive","locale":"en"},"653":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-13","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`archive`","locale":"en"},"654":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-14","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"VSIX, MSI and CAB extraction","locale":"en"},"655":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-15","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"—","locale":"en"},"656":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-16","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"catalog","locale":"en"},"657":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-17","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`catalog`","locale":"en"},"658":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-18","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Catalog parsing and package selection","locale":"en"},"659":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-19","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"foundation","locale":"en"},"660":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-20","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"download","locale":"en"},"661":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-21","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`download`","locale":"en"},"662":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-22","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Network transfers, integrity, ranges and cache","locale":"en"},"663":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-23","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"foundation","locale":"en"},"664":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-24","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"state","locale":"en"},"665":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-25","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`state`","locale":"en"},"666":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-26","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Directory discovery, named references, projects and local selection","locale":"en"},"667":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-27","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"foundation","locale":"en"},"668":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-28","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"shell","locale":"en"},"669":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-29","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`shell`","locale":"en"},"670":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-30","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Sessions, scripts and startup integration","locale":"en"},"671":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-31","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"foundation, state","locale":"en"},"672":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-32","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"engine","locale":"en"},"673":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-33","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`engine`","locale":"en"},"674":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-34","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Staged installation, publication, import, diagnosis and uninstall","locale":"en"},"675":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-35","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"foundation, archive, catalog, download, state","locale":"en"},"676":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-36","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"application","locale":"en"},"677":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-37","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`cli`, `commands`, `config`, `logging`, `runtime`, `self_uninstall`, `upgrade`","locale":"en"},"678":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-38","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Command line, configuration, self-update and self-uninstall","locale":"en"},"679":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-39","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"all layers","locale":"en"},"680":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-40","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`file_usage` encapsulates Windows Restart Manager for individual files and directory trees.\nInstallation replacement, leftover directory cleanup, toolchain uninstall, cache cleanup,\nupdate backup removal and self-uninstall metadata removal share it. Callers retain operation\nlocks and preview handling. The module skips links, never closes its own process and leaves\nother platforms using ordinary file operations.","locale":"en"},"681":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-41","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"The unpublished `test-support` crate holds synthetic payloads, HTTP fixtures and shell\nprobes for tests. `cargo xtask check` enforces the structure and runs in CI:","locale":"en"},"682":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-42","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"no dependency cycles between sibling modules at any depth, including code for other\nplatforms; test-only code is exempt;","locale":"en"},"683":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-43","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"the layer directions in the table;","locale":"en"},"684":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-44","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"parent modules (`lib.rs` and any file with child modules) contain only `mod`\ndeclarations and re-exports, so implementation lives in leaf modules.","locale":"en"},"685":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-45","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"Each managed combination occupies `<toolchains-dir>/<source>/msvc-<download ID>_sdk-<ID or none>_host-<host>_target-<target>`. Local commands discover directories and check a small set of required files. Directory names retain download IDs; actual compiler and SDK versions come from the extracted tree. Custom source identity is a stable SHA-256 of the manifest URL, independent of changing manifest contents.","locale":"en"},"686":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-46","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"MSBuild combinations insert `_msbuild-<version>` before `_host-<host>_target-<target>`. `catalog/msbuild` selects explicit VS 2022/2026 C++ package sets without recursively installing arbitrary VS dependencies. Payload roles distinguish toolset, SDK and MSBuild; FileTracker's MSI is extracted separately and arranged beside the private engine. The foundation `msbuild` module generates local props/targets from source templates, records the engine package version and defines required-file checks. It does not modify upstream targets, write registry entries or invoke system installers.","locale":"en"},"687":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-47","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture","content":"`references/<name>.json` stores a managed directory key or an external path with fixed component versions. References do not prove installation exists, and one broken reference does not hide other tools. There is no installation database, file receipt or JSON recovery journal. Shell startup ownership records remain separate. Library installation options are explicit and do not load global user configuration.","locale":"en"},"688":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-48","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture#extraction-and-publication","content":"Opening a VSIX identifies the compiler directory version, normalizes output paths and\ncounts files together. Extraction reuses this metadata and streams files directly into\nthe installation transaction's private staging tree. MSI file, directory, component and\nmedia mappings are prepared once for counting and extraction; discovering CAB downloads\nstill requires an earlier read of the MSI media table.","locale":"en"},"689":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-49","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture#extraction-and-publication","content":"CAB files are read in offset order within each compressed folder, keeping one decoder\nalive across files instead of restarting it for every file. The backend is pinned to\n`cab-superewald 0.6.1`, which exposes folder readers and retains Stored, MSZIP and LZX\ndecoding. Only one cabinet is open at a time, and file contents are streamed rather than\nbuffered in full.","locale":"en"},"690":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-50","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture#extraction-and-publication","content":"SDK scratch directories live inside the installation transaction. Arranging `Windows Kits`\ntherefore moves data on the same volume instead of copying the whole SDK from a download\nworkspace on another drive. Failed extraction discards the staging tree; individual files\ndo not need temporary siblings or handling for binaries held open by a running compiler.","locale":"en"},"691":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-51","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture#extraction-and-publication","content":"Download integrity, archive checksums and output path checks remain enabled. Before publication, the engine checks actual versions and required compiler, header and library files. It does not generate a full file inventory or hash the installed tree.","locale":"en"},"692":{"id":"/en/docs/architecture-52","page_id":"/en/docs/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/architecture#extraction-and-publication","content":"The target lock protects preparation in a sibling `.<name>.stage` directory on the destination volume. Publication renames the old tree to `.old`, moves the new tree into place, then removes the old tree. Failed preparation preserves existing files. The next install cleans interrupted staging and restores `.old` when the final directory is missing; ordinary reuse also runs this cleanup. Missing managed directories or required files trigger installation. Use `--reinstall` for damage beyond the quick required-file checks.","locale":"en"},"693":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","type":"page","content":"Bash and Zsh","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Shell integration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","locale":"en"},"694":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-0","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","content":"Load hooks, handle native Windows paths and configure login startup files.","locale":"en"},"695":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-1","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh#windows-paths","content":"Windows paths","locale":"en"},"696":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-2","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh#persistent-entries","content":"Persistent entries","locale":"en"},"697":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-3","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","content":"Omitting `--shell` detects the calling shell. When explicitly generating a script, choose `--shell bash` or `--shell zsh` to match the shell that will source it.","locale":"en"},"698":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-4","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh#windows-paths","content":"A native executable path such as `D:\\Tools\\hanamori.exe` is not a POSIX command path. Generated hooks use the current MSYS runtime’s `cygpath -u` before invoking it. Keep a working `cygpath` on PATH; a failed conversion stops execution.","locale":"en"},"699":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-5","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh#windows-paths","content":"After replacing an old hook, call the new executable directly to regenerate and load `env`, or rerun `shell init` to update persistent entries. For example, invoke `/d/Tools/hanamori.exe` in Git Bash/Zsh, quoting paths containing spaces. INCLUDE/LIB consumed by the compiler retain Windows syntax; do not convert every variable to POSIX paths.","locale":"en"},"700":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-6","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh#persistent-entries","content":"Default Bash setup maintains `.bashrc` and a login-profile bridge without repeating user settings in login/non-login sessions. With no usable login file, it creates the lowest-priority `.profile`. Deinitialization can delete that generated file if it becomes empty, retaining user additions. Zsh respects `ZDOTDIR`; explicit `--profile` takes precedence.","locale":"en"},"701":{"id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh-7","page_id":"/en/docs/bash-zsh","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/bash-zsh#persistent-entries","content":"Supporting these shells does not mean MSVC executes natively on Linux/macOS. See platform support.","locale":"en"},"702":{"id":"/en/docs/build","page_id":"/en/docs/build","type":"page","content":"Install Hanamori or build from source","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/build","locale":"en"},"703":{"id":"/en/docs/build-0","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build","content":"Install with PowerShell, download a portable executable, or build with Rust.","locale":"en"},"704":{"id":"/en/docs/build-1","page_id":"/en/docs/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"One-command installation","locale":"en"},"705":{"id":"/en/docs/build-2","page_id":"/en/docs/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"MSYS2 and Git Bash","locale":"en"},"706":{"id":"/en/docs/build-3","page_id":"/en/docs/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/build#build-from-source","content":"Build from source","locale":"en"},"707":{"id":"/en/docs/build-4","page_id":"/en/docs/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/build#portable-installation","content":"Portable installation","locale":"en"},"708":{"id":"/en/docs/build-5","page_id":"/en/docs/build","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/build#arm64-program-builds","content":"ARM64 program builds","locale":"en"},"709":{"id":"/en/docs/build-6","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Run in Windows PowerShell 5.1 or PowerShell 7 on Windows x64 / ARM64:","locale":"en"},"710":{"id":"/en/docs/build-7","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"The script downloads the latest stable release, checks its SHA-256, size and reported version, and installs `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori\\bin\\hanamori.exe`. It adds the directory to your user PATH and initializes the current PowerShell profile and session with completions. It requires no administrator privileges and downloads no toolchains. Running inline takes effect immediately; running in a child process requires opening a new terminal afterward.","locale":"en"},"711":{"id":"/en/docs/build-8","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"To choose a release or executable directory:","locale":"en"},"712":{"id":"/en/docs/build-9","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"You can also set `HANAMORI_INSTALL_DIR` to the directory that should contain `hanamori.exe`:","locale":"en"},"713":{"id":"/en/docs/build-10","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"The priority is `-InstallDir`, then `HANAMORI_INSTALL_DIR`, then `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori\\bin`. An unset or empty environment variable uses the default directory.","locale":"en"},"714":{"id":"/en/docs/build-11","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Parameter","locale":"en"},"715":{"id":"/en/docs/build-12","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"716":{"id":"/en/docs/build-13","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"`-Version`","locale":"en"},"717":{"id":"/en/docs/build-14","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"`latest` or a version, with an optional `v` prefix","locale":"en"},"718":{"id":"/en/docs/build-15","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"`-InstallDir`","locale":"en"},"719":{"id":"/en/docs/build-16","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Directory containing `hanamori.exe`","locale":"en"},"720":{"id":"/en/docs/build-17","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"`-NoPathUpdate`","locale":"en"},"721":{"id":"/en/docs/build-18","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Skip user and process PATH configuration","locale":"en"},"722":{"id":"/en/docs/build-19","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"`-NoShell`","locale":"en"},"723":{"id":"/en/docs/build-20","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Skip persistent and current-session PowerShell integration","locale":"en"},"724":{"id":"/en/docs/build-21","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Repeat installation replaces the executable and reuses existing configuration. Download or verification failures preserve the previous executable. `HANAMORI_HOME` still selects manager data, independently of the executable directory. Existing PATH entries and profile content are preserved. The installer warns about restrictive execution policies without changing them. Configure other shells through the shell integration guide.","locale":"en"},"725":{"id":"/en/docs/build-22","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#one-command-installation","content":"Install toolchains when needed with `hanamori install latest --name stable`. Use `hanamori upgrade` for later updates and `hanamori self uninstall` for removal. Self uninstall removes installer-owned PATH entries using the adjacent `.install.json` receipt.","locale":"en"},"726":{"id":"/en/docs/build-23","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"Run in MSYS2 or Git Bash on Windows x64 / ARM64:","locale":"en"},"727":{"id":"/en/docs/build-24","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"The Bash installer reuses the PowerShell download, verification and user PATH setup, then invokes `hanamori shell init --shell bash` with the actual Bash runtime to configure `.bashrc`, login startup and completions. It defaults to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori\\bin`, installs no toolchains and leaves PowerShell profiles unchanged.","locale":"en"},"728":{"id":"/en/docs/build-25","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"It requires `cygpath`, `curl` and Windows PowerShell or PowerShell 7. If PowerShell is absent from the MSYS2 PATH, the script checks the Windows system directory. From a checkout, run `bash install.sh` to use the adjacent `install.ps1`.","locale":"en"},"729":{"id":"/en/docs/build-26","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"Options are `--version`, `--install-dir`, `--no-path-update` and `--no-shell`. Installation directories accept MSYS or Windows paths. `--no-shell` skips Bash startup and completion setup; `--no-path-update` skips user PATH configuration.","locale":"en"},"730":{"id":"/en/docs/build-27","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"Bash also supports `HANAMORI_INSTALL_DIR`, with `--install-dir` taking precedence. An unset or empty variable uses the default directory. For a piped installation, pass the variable to `bash`:","locale":"en"},"731":{"id":"/en/docs/build-28","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#msys2-and-git-bash","content":"`curl | bash` runs in a child process. Open a new Bash terminal afterward, or run the printed hook command to use Hanamori immediately in the current terminal. MSYS2 may rebuild PATH at startup; the Bash hook invokes Hanamori by its absolute path.","locale":"en"},"732":{"id":"/en/docs/build-29","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#build-from-source","content":"On Windows the executable is `target/release/hanamori.exe`. No `aria2c`, `msiexec`, or\nVisual Studio installation is needed to run the installer. Building requires Rust and a linker for the chosen target; the Windows MSVC target needs the corresponding build tools.\nThe repository is licyk/Hanamori.","locale":"en"},"733":{"id":"/en/docs/build-30","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#build-from-source","content":"The release workflow produces\nEXE and ZIP assets for `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` and `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, named\n`hanamori-<target>.exe` and `hanamori-<target>.zip`. The ZIP entry is `hanamori.exe`.","locale":"en"},"734":{"id":"/en/docs/build-31","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#portable-installation","content":"Use the download page to choose a release for your architecture. Rename the standalone EXE to `hanamori.exe`, or extract it from the ZIP, and place it in a tools directory such as `D:\\Tools\\Hanamori`. No Rust installation is needed to run a downloaded executable.","locale":"en"},"735":{"id":"/en/docs/build-32","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#portable-installation","content":"For the current PowerShell session:","locale":"en"},"736":{"id":"/en/docs/build-33","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#portable-installation","content":"For future sessions, add that directory to your user PATH through Windows Environment Variables. Shell initialization creates a command hook; it does not install the executable or permanently edit PATH.","locale":"en"},"737":{"id":"/en/docs/build-34","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#portable-installation","content":"Self-update supports the Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC build; a different development target does not establish support for installing native MSVC on that host.","locale":"en"},"738":{"id":"/en/docs/build-35","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#arm64-program-builds","content":"The installer chooses the native Windows architecture, including when launched from an emulated shell. Override with PowerShell `-Architecture x64` / `-Architecture arm64`, or Bash `--architecture x64` / `--architecture arm64`. This selects Hanamori itself; `hanamori install --arch HOST/TARGET` selects the compiler independently.","locale":"en"},"739":{"id":"/en/docs/build-36","page_id":"/en/docs/build","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/build#arm64-program-builds","content":"ARM64 releases provide `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` and `.zip`; the ZIP contains `hanamori.exe`. Source builds use `cargo build --release --target aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` with the corresponding MSVC linker.","locale":"en"},"740":{"id":"/en/docs/cache","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","type":"page","content":"Downloads, cache and proxy","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cache","locale":"en"},"741":{"id":"/en/docs/cache-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cache","content":"Separate complete payload caching from resumable download workspaces.","locale":"en"},"742":{"id":"/en/docs/cache-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cache","content":"Complete payloads are stored by SHA-256 content identity after verification. Corrupt entries are fetched again. Independent installations can reuse these files without sharing installed SDK directories.","locale":"en"},"743":{"id":"/en/docs/cache-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cache","content":"`--download-dir` selects a separate persistent workspace for unfinished, resumable downloads. It is not the complete cache. The default workspace is temporary; selecting `--cache-dir` does not preserve incomplete fragments automatically.","locale":"en"},"744":{"id":"/en/docs/cache-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cache","content":"`--file-workers` controls concurrent payloads; `--connections` controls connections per payload. Defaults are 4 and 8. `--mirror` changes the payload host/base path with fallback to the original URL. See configuration for fields and precedence.","locale":"en"},"745":{"id":"/en/docs/cache-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cache","content":"Cleanup recognizes complete files only in the fixed SHA-256 namespace. It preserves unknown files, partial downloads, directories and locks. Entries locked by another Hanamori operation are skipped. On Windows, after acquiring the cache lock, a deletion blocked by file usage closes that file's users through Windows Restart Manager and retries. Incomplete cleanup returns a nonzero status and reports completed removals. Resolve contention and retry. It does not modify toolchains or references or persistent workspaces. Previews take no locks, write no files and close no processes.","locale":"en"},"746":{"id":"/en/docs/cache-5","page_id":"/en/docs/cache","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cache","content":"Self-update uses GitHub API and Release assets with the same proxy configuration, but does not use the toolchain mirror, cache or download directory.","locale":"en"},"747":{"id":"/en/docs/cli","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"page","content":"Command reference","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli","locale":"en"},"748":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"All public commands, defaults, conflicts and output conventions.","locale":"en"},"749":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Global options","locale":"en"},"750":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Installation and remote catalogs","locale":"en"},"751":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Local directories and selection","locale":"en"},"752":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-4","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"Shell commands","locale":"en"},"753":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-5","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Lifecycle and cleanup","locale":"en"},"754":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-6","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cli#output-conventions","content":"Output conventions","locale":"en"},"755":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-7","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli","content":"This page follows the current Clap definitions. See individual guides for environment and directory semantics. `hanamori --help` and `hanamori COMMAND --help` describe the installed build. There is no `run` alias.","locale":"en"},"756":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-8","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#global-options","content":"Public commands accept `--manager-dir PATH`, `--toolchains-dir PATH`, `--cache-dir PATH`, `--download-dir PATH`, `--proxy URL`, `--mirror URL`, `--file-workers N`, `--connections N` and `--log FILTER`. Only consumed settings are resolved. See configuration for defaults, ranges and environment mappings. `-h/--help` prints help; top-level `-V/--version` prints the version.","locale":"en"},"757":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-9","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Installation includes MSVC + Windows SDK + MSBuild by default. Install help groups destination, versions and components, installation behavior, and catalog options.","locale":"en"},"758":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-10","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Command/option","locale":"en"},"759":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-11","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"760":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-12","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`install [VERSION]`","locale":"en"},"761":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-13","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Managed directory key, actual version/prefix or latest; project constraints apply; otherwise chooses the channel’s latest","locale":"en"},"762":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-14","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--dir/-d PATH`","locale":"en"},"763":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-15","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Exact final directory instead of independent managed storage","locale":"en"},"764":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-16","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--name ALIAS`","locale":"en"},"765":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-17","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Fixed alias; does not activate or change default","locale":"en"},"766":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-18","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--toolset-id ID`","locale":"en"},"767":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-19","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Exact download ID; conflicts with positional VERSION","locale":"en"},"768":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-20","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--sdk VER`","locale":"en"},"769":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-21","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Actual SDK version; conflicts with sdk-id and no-sdk","locale":"en"},"770":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-22","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--sdk-id ID`","locale":"en"},"771":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-23","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"SDK download ID; conflicts with sdk and no-sdk","locale":"en"},"772":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-24","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--no-sdk`","locale":"en"},"773":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-25","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Exclude the SDK and, by default, MSBuild; add `--no-msbuild` if the project explicitly requires MSBuild","locale":"en"},"774":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-26","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--msbuild`","locale":"en"},"775":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-27","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Explicitly enable MSBuild, overriding the project; enabled with the SDK by default, for VS 2022 v143 and VS 2026 v145; conflicts with `--no-sdk` and `--no-msbuild`","locale":"en"},"776":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-28","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--no-msbuild`","locale":"en"},"777":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-29","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Disable MSBuild, overriding the default and the project; keeps the compiler and SDK by default","locale":"en"},"778":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-30","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--reinstall`","locale":"en"},"779":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-31","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Replace the whole tree; required for a nonempty external directory","locale":"en"},"780":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-32","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--arch ARCH`","locale":"en"},"781":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-33","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`x64/x64`, `x64/arm64`, `arm64/x64`, `arm64/arm64`; explicit option → project → native Windows architecture","locale":"en"},"782":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-34","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--dry-run`","locale":"en"},"783":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-35","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"May query manifests; no payload download, installation, reference or workspace writes","locale":"en"},"784":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-36","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`list-remote`","locale":"en"},"785":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-37","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Defaults to VS 2026; `--all` queries VS 2022 and 2026; optional `--toolset-id ID` inspects a selected toolset; supports `--json`","locale":"en"},"786":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-38","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"Both commands accept `--vs-version 2022/2026` (aliases 17/18; default 2026), `--channel release/preview` (aliases stable/insiders; default release), `--manifest URL` (conflicts with both) and `--strict-manifest-integrity`. Install has no `--json` option.","locale":"en"},"787":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-39","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`list-remote --all` groups toolsets and SDKs by VS 2022 and VS 2026, and expands the latest toolset’s packages in each group. It queries release channels by default. Add `--channel preview` (or `insiders`) to query both preview channels instead, without mixing release channels into the result. Identical IDs remain in their source groups. `--all` conflicts with `--vs-version`, `--manifest`, and `--toolset-id`. “All” covers versions still offered by the selected channels for the two supported VS generations, not every historical version Microsoft has ever published.","locale":"en"},"788":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-40","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#installation-and-remote-catalogs","content":"`--all --json` returns `{ \"catalogs\": [...] }`. Each entry includes `vs_version`, `channel`, `manifest_url`, and the existing single-source fields `toolsets`, `sdks`, `selected_toolset_id`, and `packages`. A failure in either source fails the whole command without printing a partial list. The warning/strict manifest-integrity policy applies to both sources.","locale":"en"},"789":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-41","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Command","locale":"en"},"790":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-42","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Parameters and result","locale":"en"},"791":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-43","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`list [--json]`","locale":"en"},"792":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-44","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Discovered directories, aliases, actual versions and availability; no network","locale":"en"},"793":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-45","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`current [--json]`","locale":"en"},"794":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-46","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Current fixed session snapshot, without reselecting project/default","locale":"en"},"795":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-47","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`alias [SELECTOR NAME] [--json]`","locale":"en"},"796":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-48","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Both positionals together assign; otherwise lists mappings","locale":"en"},"797":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-49","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`default [SELECTOR] [--json]`","locale":"en"},"798":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-50","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Set or query a fixed default installation","locale":"en"},"799":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-51","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`unalias NAME`","locale":"en"},"800":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-52","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Remove an alias; absent names are harmless","locale":"en"},"801":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-53","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`use [SELECTOR]`","locale":"en"},"802":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-54","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Change this shell through a loaded hook; accepts direct-directory options below","locale":"en"},"803":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-55","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`deactivate`","locale":"en"},"804":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-56","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Restore this shell through the hook","locale":"en"},"805":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-57","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"`exec [--using SELECTOR] -- COMMAND [ARGS...]`","locale":"en"},"806":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-58","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Prepare and run a child, preserving its status; accepts directory options","locale":"en"},"807":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-59","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"SELECTOR is a full managed directory key, external reference key (`@NAME`), alias or unique actual-version prefix. Local selection does not accept latest. Without an explicit choice, use the nearest project, then default.","locale":"en"},"808":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-60","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#local-directories-and-selection","content":"Direct-directory options are `--dir/-d PATH`, `--toolset VER`, `--sdk VER`, `--no-sdk` and `--arch HOST/TARGET`. These selectors require dir, and sdk conflicts with no-sdk. Explicit SELECTOR or exec’s using conflicts with all directory options. Component selectors use actual directory versions.","locale":"en"},"809":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-61","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"Command","locale":"en"},"810":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-62","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"Options","locale":"en"},"811":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-63","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`completions`","locale":"en"},"812":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-64","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`--shell/-s SHELL`, `--output/-o PATH`; generates completion without loading a toolchain hook","locale":"en"},"813":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-65","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`env`","locale":"en"},"814":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-66","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`--shell/-s SHELL`, `--output/-o PATH`, `--auto-activate`, `--use-on-cd`, `--completions`, hook toolchain directory defaults","locale":"en"},"815":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-67","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`shell init`","locale":"en"},"816":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-68","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`--shell/-s`, `--profile PATH` or `--shell-executable PATH`, `--auto-activate`, `--use-on-cd`, `--completions`, `--dry-run`, hook toolchain directory defaults","locale":"en"},"817":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-69","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`shell deinit`","locale":"en"},"818":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-70","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`--shell/-s`, `--profile` or `--shell-executable`, `--dry-run`","locale":"en"},"819":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-71","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`shell activate [SELECTOR]`","locale":"en"},"820":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-72","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"Direct-directory options, `--shell/-s`, `--output/-o` or `--plain`","locale":"en"},"821":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-73","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`shell deactivate`","locale":"en"},"822":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-74","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`--shell/-s`, `--output/-o`","locale":"en"},"823":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-75","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"SHELL is powershell, bash, zsh or cmd; omitted values trigger detection. Plain skips detection and conflicts with shell/output. Profile and shell-executable conflict; CMD accepts neither.","locale":"en"},"824":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-76","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"Hook directory defaults use `--dir PATH` (no short `-d` here), `--toolset VER`, `--sdk VER` or `--no-sdk`. Component options require dir; sdk and no-sdk conflict. Each command selects the manager through `--manager-dir`, `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform default. Hook, completion and startup generation do not save a manager directory. Output defaults to stdout; when writing CMD output to a file, its path must end in `.cmd/.bat`. Hidden dispatch/run subcommands serve hooks, not the public interface.","locale":"en"},"825":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-77","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#shell-commands","content":"`completions`, `env --completions` and `shell init --completions` support PowerShell, Bash and Zsh; CMD returns an explicit error. Completion is opt-in, reads only manager/toolchain storage configuration and does not use the network, and requires `compinit` in Zsh. Local selectors, existing aliases and component versions in an explicit directory are completed dynamically using the current command/environment manager selection. See terminal completion for value/path support and PowerShell limitations.","locale":"en"},"826":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-78","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Command","locale":"en"},"827":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-79","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Required parameters and options","locale":"en"},"828":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-80","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`import`","locale":"en"},"829":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-81","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Required `--dir/-d PATH --name NAME`; optional toolset, sdk or no-sdk, and json","locale":"en"},"830":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-82","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`remove NAME`","locale":"en"},"831":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-83","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`--dry-run`, `--json`; delete a named reference and preserve files","locale":"en"},"832":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-84","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`uninstall SELECTOR`","locale":"en"},"833":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-85","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`--dry-run`, `--json`; delete an entire managed directory and its references; external directories are rejected","locale":"en"},"834":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-86","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`doctor`","locale":"en"},"835":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-87","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`--dir PATH`, `--json`; read-only, nonzero when errors exist","locale":"en"},"836":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-88","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`cache clean`","locale":"en"},"837":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-89","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`--dry-run`, `--json`; clean idle complete cache payloads","locale":"en"},"838":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-90","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`config show`","locale":"en"},"839":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-91","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Configuration table by default; `--resolved` includes sources and derived paths; `--json` prints JSON","locale":"en"},"840":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-92","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`upgrade`","locale":"en"},"841":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-93","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Mutually exclusive `--check` or `--force`; Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC only","locale":"en"},"842":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-94","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`self uninstall`","locale":"en"},"843":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-95","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"`--dry-run`, `--purge`; preserves manager data by default; no json","locale":"en"},"844":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-96","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#lifecycle-and-cleanup","content":"Import has no dry-run option; importing the same name updates that reference. Catalog queries and installation may access the network; local management does not automatically install. Do not assume every command supports json or dry-run.","locale":"en"},"845":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-97","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-conventions","content":"Information commands use aligned tables or labeled fields by default. `list` marks active and default entries, while `alias` and `default` show target status; directory paths appear on their own lines. Use the command's `--json` option for programmatic access. Disabling logging does not hide query results.","locale":"en"},"846":{"id":"/en/docs/cli-98","page_id":"/en/docs/cli","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cli#output-conventions","content":"Logs use stderr; JSON and generated scripts use stdout. Exec’s child inherits streams. Failures return nonzero; do not source output from failed generation. Doctor still fails when its JSON reports errors. Previews can list blockers; execution requires resolving them. On Windows, scheduling self removal is not proof that the executable has already been deleted: the helper reports its own result.","locale":"en"},"847":{"id":"/en/docs/cmd","page_id":"/en/docs/cmd","type":"page","content":"CMD integration","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Shell integration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/cmd","locale":"en"},"848":{"id":"/en/docs/cmd-0","page_id":"/en/docs/cmd","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cmd","content":"Experimental batch entry, DOSKEY and current-user AutoRun.","locale":"en"},"849":{"id":"/en/docs/cmd-1","page_id":"/en/docs/cmd","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cmd","content":"CMD uses a batch entry and DOSKEY macro, not POSIX evaluation. Inside another batch file,\nuse `call \"%_HANAMORI_CMD_ENTRY%\" use stable` rather than relying on interactive DOSKEY.\nTo maintain the current user's AutoRun entry on native Windows:","locale":"en"},"850":{"id":"/en/docs/cmd-2","page_id":"/en/docs/cmd","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cmd","content":"`cmd /d` bypasses AutoRun; explicitly call the generated entry in that case. Existing\nAutoRun content is preserved. `--profile` and `--shell-executable` are not CMD registry\nselectors. Loader files are retained for open sessions after deinit. Native acceptance\nof code pages, quoting, AutoRun and interactive behavior remains a separate gate.","locale":"en"},"851":{"id":"/en/docs/cmd-3","page_id":"/en/docs/cmd","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/cmd","content":"`hanamori.exe shell init --shell cmd --use-on-cd` selects a project/default toolchain at\nstartup and installs an interactive `cd` DOSKEY macro to reselect after successful directory\nchanges. It replaces an existing `cd` macro. It does not cover `chdir`, `pushd/popd`, drive\nswitches or directory changes inside batch scripts; use `hanamori exec` / `hanamori run`\nfor scripts. Portable `env --shell cmd` entries do not support this option; persistent\ninitialization is required.","locale":"en"},"852":{"id":"/en/docs/completions","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"page","content":"Terminal completion","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Shell integration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions","locale":"en"},"853":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-0","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions","content":"Enable command, option and path completion in PowerShell, Bash and Zsh.","locale":"en"},"854":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-1","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-with-shell-initialization","content":"Enable with shell initialization","locale":"en"},"855":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-2","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-in-this-session-only","content":"Enable in this session only","locale":"en"},"856":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-3","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions#generate-a-standalone-script","content":"Generate a standalone script","locale":"en"},"857":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-4","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Local dynamic candidates","locale":"en"},"858":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-5","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Supported completion","locale":"en"},"859":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-6","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/completions#removal-and-troubleshooting","content":"Removal and troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"860":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-7","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions","content":"Hanamori generates completion scripts from the current build's command definitions. Tab completes public commands, nested subcommands and options. Generation needs no installed toolchain, network access or manager configuration.","locale":"en"},"861":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-8","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-with-shell-initialization","content":"Omitting `--shell` detects the calling shell; you can explicitly select `powershell`, `bash` or `zsh`. As with normal initialization, use `--profile PATH` or `--shell-executable PATH` to select the startup file/runtime, and `--dry-run` to preview changes.","locale":"en"},"862":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-9","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-with-shell-initialization","content":"Open a new terminal or follow the printed profile reload instruction. The startup block stores a loader that generates completion from the executable on each startup, so new sessions use the updated command definitions after an upgrade. Normal `shell init` does not enable completion. Keep `--completions` when updating the managed block; omitting it switches the block back to loading only the hook.","locale":"en"},"863":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-10","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-with-shell-initialization","content":"In Zsh, place the Hanamori startup block after `compinit` or your framework's completion initialization. If initialization is missing, Hanamori prints a hint and skips completion while keeping the toolchain hook usable. It does not run `compinit` for you.","locale":"en"},"864":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-11","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-in-this-session-only","content":"PowerShell:","locale":"en"},"865":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-12","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-in-this-session-only","content":"Bash:","locale":"en"},"866":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-13","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-in-this-session-only","content":"Zsh:","locale":"en"},"867":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-14","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#enable-in-this-session-only","content":"These commands load both the `use/deactivate` hook and completion. To load completion alone, replace `env --completions` with `completions`; it neither installs an environment hook nor activates a toolchain.","locale":"en"},"868":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-15","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#generate-a-standalone-script","content":"Without `--shell/-s`, detection selects the calling shell or asks you to specify it. Without `--output/-o`, stdout contains only the registration script. Load a saved file in its matching shell. The Zsh output is intended for explicit sourcing; copying it into system completion directories is unnecessary. Manually saved scripts do not update automatically: regenerate and reload them after upgrading, and open a new terminal to clear old completion definitions.","locale":"en"},"869":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-16","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#generate-a-standalone-script","content":"Both `hanamori` and `hanamori.exe` are registered, including the function installed by the hook. An executable outside PATH can still generate scripts when invoked by its path. Use a POSIX path understood by your shell in Windows Bash/Zsh.","locale":"en"},"870":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-17","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"All three shells support these local candidates. The next Tab press reads changes after an installation, import or alias update without regenerating the script.","locale":"en"},"871":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-18","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Input position","locale":"en"},"872":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-19","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Candidates","locale":"en"},"873":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-20","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"First positional argument of `use`, `default`, `alias`","locale":"en"},"874":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-21","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Managed directory keys, external reference keys, existing aliases (including default), unambiguous full MSVC directory versions","locale":"en"},"875":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-22","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Selectors for `exec --using`, `shell activate`","locale":"en"},"876":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-23","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Same as above","locale":"en"},"877":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-24","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"`remove`, `unalias`","locale":"en"},"878":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-25","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Existing named references","locale":"en"},"879":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-26","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"`uninstall`","locale":"en"},"880":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-27","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Usable managed directory keys, managed references and unambiguous versions","locale":"en"},"881":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-28","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"`--dir PATH --toolset`","locale":"en"},"882":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-29","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"MSVC directory versions in the specified directory","locale":"en"},"883":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-30","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"`--dir PATH --sdk`","locale":"en"},"884":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-31","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"SDK directory versions in the specified directory; none with `--no-sdk`","locale":"en"},"885":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-32","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Directory version completion applies to `use`, `exec`, `import`, `env`, `shell activate` and `shell init`, including unregistered directories. These are actual installed versions such as `14.44.35207` and `10.0.26100.0`, not remote download IDs. The second argument of `alias` creates a new name and does not suggest selectors. Installation and remote catalog commands do not mix in local versions either.","locale":"en"},"886":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-33","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"When multiple installations share an MSVC version, for example with different SDKs, that version cannot select an installation uniquely. Completion offers exact directory keys and references instead. Activation candidates exclude unusable directories; remove/unalias can still suggest dangling references. Completion changes no files and does not replace execution-time checks.","locale":"en"},"887":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-34","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Manager selection consistently follows the already entered `--manager-dir`, then `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform default (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori` on Windows). Functions, direct executable calls and completion use the same rule. Changing HOME affects the next completion. A generation-time `--manager-dir` is not stored as a fallback manager.","locale":"en"},"888":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-35","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"`--using=prefix` and quoted/escaped paths are supported. Completion interprets literal arguments before the cursor without executing variable expansions or command expressions. Use `HANAMORI_HOME` when selecting a manager through such expressions.","locale":"en"},"889":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-36","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#local-dynamic-candidates","content":"Candidate lookup resolves `toolchains_dir` from CLI, environment, configuration and defaults. It does not parse unrelated proxy/log settings or project files, download manifests, write files or acquire locks. One malformed reference is skipped without hiding other installations. Unreadable storage suppresses relevant local candidates while static completion remains available. Manually saved scripts invoke the executable path used at generation time; regenerate them if you move the program.","locale":"en"},"890":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-37","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Content","locale":"en"},"891":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-38","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"892":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-39","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Commands and options","locale":"en"},"893":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-40","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Supported in PowerShell, Bash and Zsh, including nested commands such as `shell init`, `cache clean` and `self uninstall`","locale":"en"},"894":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-41","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Fixed values","locale":"en"},"895":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-42","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Bash/Zsh offer declared choices for options such as `--vs-version`, `--channel` and `--shell`","locale":"en"},"896":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-43","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Files and directories","locale":"en"},"897":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-44","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Bash/Zsh use path hints and shell filename completion; the shell handles spaces","locale":"en"},"898":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-45","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"PowerShell","locale":"en"},"899":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-46","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Supports the local dynamic candidates above; fixed enum values and ordinary paths retain static-generator limitations, including context recognition with leading global options","locale":"en"},"900":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-47","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Directory keys, aliases and installed versions","locale":"en"},"901":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-48","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Scan managed directories, references or the explicit directory for the relevant input position","locale":"en"},"902":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-49","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Remote toolset and SDK IDs","locale":"en"},"903":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-50","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"No network lookups; inspect `list-remote` instead","locale":"en"},"904":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-51","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Arguments after `exec --`","locale":"en"},"905":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-52","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"No Hanamori option suggestions; completion of the child program's arguments is outside this feature","locale":"en"},"906":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-53","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"CMD / Fish","locale":"en"},"907":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-54","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Not currently provided; requesting CMD completion returns an explicit error","locale":"en"},"908":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-55","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#supported-completion","content":"Suggestions do not replace command argument validation. Internal `shell dispatch`, `shell cmd-dispatch` and `shell run` commands are excluded.","locale":"en"},"909":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-56","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#removal-and-troubleshooting","content":"`hanamori shell deinit` removes the managed startup block. `self uninstall` uses the same ownership records to clean it up. Loaded functions and completion remain in the current session until you restart the shell. Remove manually saved completion files and handwritten `source` entries yourself.","locale":"en"},"910":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-57","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#removal-and-troubleshooting","content":"If no candidates appear, verify that you loaded the script for the correct shell and that your binary provides `completions`. In Zsh, initialize completion and reload the script if you see the `compinit` hint. For missing local candidates, check manager selection and diagnose directories and references with `list --json` / `doctor --json`; completion itself keeps these errors quiet. After an upgrade, regenerate manual scripts or open a new terminal using the startup loader.","locale":"en"},"911":{"id":"/en/docs/completions-58","page_id":"/en/docs/completions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/completions#removal-and-troubleshooting","content":"See startup profiles, shell integration and troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"912":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration and storage","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/configuration","locale":"en"},"913":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-0","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"Global options, environment variables, precedence and directory layout.","locale":"en"},"914":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-1","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"The manager directory is chosen by `--manager-dir`, then `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform\nlocal-data directory under `Hanamori`. Read `<manager>/config.json` after choosing it:","locale":"en"},"915":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-2","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"On Windows, the default is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori`. Shell hooks, startup loaders and completion use this same selection rule; they do not save a separate manager binding. Set `HANAMORI_HOME` before loading the hook when you want a custom directory.","locale":"en"},"916":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-3","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"Unknown fields are ignored; optional `schema_version` is currently `1`. Other values use\nexplicit CLI > nonempty environment variable > configuration file > default. Manager\nlocation is not read back from its own configuration file.","locale":"en"},"917":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-4","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"CLI/config field","locale":"en"},"918":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-5","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"Environment","locale":"en"},"919":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-6","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"Default","locale":"en"},"920":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-7","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--toolchains-dir` / `toolchains_dir`","locale":"en"},"921":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-8","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_TOOLCHAINS_DIR`","locale":"en"},"922":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-9","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`<manager>/toolchains`","locale":"en"},"923":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-10","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--cache-dir` / `cache_dir`","locale":"en"},"924":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-11","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_CACHE_DIR`","locale":"en"},"925":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-12","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`<manager>/cache`","locale":"en"},"926":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-13","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--download-dir` / `download_dir`","locale":"en"},"927":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-14","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_DOWNLOAD_DIR`","locale":"en"},"928":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-15","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"Temporary workspace","locale":"en"},"929":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-16","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--proxy` / `proxy`","locale":"en"},"930":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-17","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_PROXY`","locale":"en"},"931":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-18","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"None","locale":"en"},"932":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-19","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--mirror` / `mirror`","locale":"en"},"933":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-20","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_MIRROR`","locale":"en"},"934":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-21","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"None","locale":"en"},"935":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-22","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--file-workers` / `file_workers`","locale":"en"},"936":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-23","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_FILE_WORKERS`","locale":"en"},"937":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-24","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"4, range 1–256","locale":"en"},"938":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-25","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--connections` / `connections`","locale":"en"},"939":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-26","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_CONNECTIONS`","locale":"en"},"940":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-27","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"8, range 1–64","locale":"en"},"941":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-28","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`--log` / `log`","locale":"en"},"942":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-29","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`HANAMORI_LOG`","locale":"en"},"943":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-30","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`info` tracing filter","locale":"en"},"944":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-31","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"CLI relative paths resolve against the invocation directory; file paths resolve against\nthe manager directory; environment paths must be absolute. Tildes and variable expressions\nare not expanded by Hanamori. Configuration queries, help and version do not create storage.\nLocal selection does not parse unused proxy/download settings. Settings contain preferences,\nnot aliases, project declarations or session state.","locale":"en"},"945":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-32","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"`config show` displays effective values in a table. `--resolved` adds source and derived-path information. Scripts should use `--json`, with `--resolved` when source information is needed.\nThe complete payload cache is content-addressed by SHA-256; corrupted entries are fetched\nagain. `--download-dir` is a separate persistent workspace for unfinished/resumable downloads.\nA configured mirror changes the payload host/base; fallback uses the original payload URL.\nCache cleanup skips active or unrecognized entries and does not touch installed tools or\npersistent workspaces. Diagnostics may include complete request URLs; configure credentials\nand handle logs accordingly.","locale":"en"},"946":{"id":"/en/docs/configuration-33","page_id":"/en/docs/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/configuration","content":"All local commands and dynamic completion use the configured `toolchains_dir`. Files in `references` name targets; deleting a reference does not delete a toolchain, and deleting a toolchain does not leave a database entry that can block reinstall.","locale":"en"},"947":{"id":"/en/docs/environment","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","type":"page","content":"Environment and session reference","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/environment","locale":"en"},"948":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-0","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"Understand managed variables, switching and restoration boundaries.","locale":"en"},"949":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-1","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"Hanamori prepares PATH, INCLUDE, LIB, `CC`, `CXX`, `VCToolsVersion`, `VCToolsInstallDir`, `VCINSTALLDIR`, `VSCMD_ARG_HOST_ARCH`, `VSCMD_ARG_TGT_ARCH`, `DISTUTILS_USE_SDK`, and SDK root/bin/version variables when an SDK is selected.","locale":"en"},"950":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-2","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"The SDK tool path is `Windows Kits/10/bin/<version>/<host>`, so activation and `exec` make `rc.exe` and `mt.exe` available by name. `WindowsSdkVerBinPath` still points to the version directory without the architecture. Installation checks include both tools and their bundled DLLs; rerun the corresponding `install` command to repair missing files in a managed installation.","locale":"en"},"951":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-3","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"It does not generate `vcvarsall.bat` or `vcvars64.bat`. POSIX shells receive POSIX executable paths, while INCLUDE/LIB consumed by the compiler retain Windows paths.","locale":"en"},"952":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-4","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"`current` reports the directory key, manager, root and component versions saved by this session. It does not re-resolve changed project files or aliases. `--plain` emits `KEY=VALUE` inspection output for a selected combination; it is not a shell script to source.","locale":"en"},"953":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-5","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"Initial activation saves the environment baseline. Switching preserves that baseline, and deactivation restores original values rather than guessing PATH. `exec` uses the same preparation logic but applies it only to the child. Internal `_HANAMORI_*` state is for hooks and child processes, not user configuration; do not construct or edit it manually.","locale":"en"},"954":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-6","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"If session state is invalid, avoid stacking activations. Retain the error and inspect installation/startup settings from a clean terminal. Removing startup entries does not restore the current environment, so deactivate before uninstalling.","locale":"en"},"955":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-7","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"After updating Hanamori, a session-variable mismatch requires opening a fresh terminal from the desktop or Start menu and running `hanamori use` again. A child shell launched from the current terminal inherits the old state. This error does not indicate damaged toolchains: MSVC, SDK and MSBuild do not need reinstalling. Hanamori does not guess missing original environment values from older sessions.","locale":"en"},"956":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-8","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"An MSBuild-enabled selection additionally manages `VSINSTALLDIR`, `VCTargetsPath`, `MSBuildExtensionsPath`, `MSBuildExtensionsPath32`, `ForceImportAfterCppDefaultProps`, `ForceImportAfterCppTargets`, `UseEnv`, `DisableRegistryUse` and `PreferredToolArchitecture`, and adds its private `MSBuild/Current/Bin/amd64` to PATH. Switching to an ordinary combination clears these settings; deactivation restores their original values. The `msbuild` field in `list/current --json` records the selected version.","locale":"en"},"957":{"id":"/en/docs/environment-9","page_id":"/en/docs/environment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/environment","content":"It also sets and manages `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1` so build nodes exit after a build instead of keeping the toolchain locked and preventing reinstallation. Parallel builds remain available, but subsequent builds cannot reuse earlier nodes. This applies to newly started builds and does not stop existing resident processes.","locale":"en"},"958":{"id":"/en/docs/execution","page_id":"/en/docs/execution","type":"page","content":"Run a command","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Toolchains and execution"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/execution","locale":"en"},"959":{"id":"/en/docs/execution-0","page_id":"/en/docs/execution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/execution","content":"Prepare a compiler environment for a child process without initializing a shell.","locale":"en"},"960":{"id":"/en/docs/execution-1","page_id":"/en/docs/execution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/execution","content":"`exec` supports registered installations and explicit unregistered directories. `--using` conflicts with `--dir` and its component selectors. With neither, it resolves the nearest project file, then the default. If a directory has multiple combinations, use actual directory versions with `--toolset`, `--sdk` or `--no-sdk`.","locale":"en"},"961":{"id":"/en/docs/execution-2","page_id":"/en/docs/execution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/execution","content":"A program is required after `--`. Arguments are passed as argv, not interpreted as pipes, redirections, globs, variable expansions or shell builtins. Invoke a shell explicitly when you need those features:","locale":"en"},"962":{"id":"/en/docs/execution-3","page_id":"/en/docs/execution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/execution","content":"The child inherits stdin, stdout and stderr, and its exit status is returned to the caller. Only the child gets the prepared environment; the parent is not activated. Through a PowerShell hook, quote `'--'` to pass the separator. Windows PowerShell uses the encoded argv forwarding path to preserve empty strings and quotes.","locale":"en"},"963":{"id":"/en/docs/execution-4","page_id":"/en/docs/execution","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/execution","content":"The public command is `exec`; there is no `run` alias. This differs from activating the current shell.","locale":"en"},"964":{"id":"/en/docs","page_id":"/en/docs","type":"page","content":"Hanamori documentation","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs","locale":"en"},"965":{"id":"/en/docs-0","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Install, select and manage standalone MSVC and Windows SDK combinations.","locale":"en"},"966":{"id":"/en/docs-1","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Hanamori installs MSVC and the Windows SDK in independent directories without a Visual Studio installation. Select a toolchain by alias or project file, activate the current terminal, or prepare an environment for one build command.","locale":"en"},"967":{"id":"/en/docs-2","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Get Hanamori from the download page, or build from source.","locale":"en"},"968":{"id":"/en/docs-3","page_id":"/en/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs","content":"Each owned installation has an exclusive directory. Imports are read-only references. Selecting tools never downloads them, and installing tools does not activate the current terminal. Native compilation supports Windows x64 / ARM64 hosts and x64 / ARM64 targets; tests on other platforms do not establish MSVC execution support. See platform support.","locale":"en"},"969":{"id":"/en/docs/installation","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"page","content":"Install toolchains and select versions","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Toolchains and execution"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation","locale":"en"},"970":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-0","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Understand download IDs, actual versions and independent installations.","locale":"en"},"971":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-1","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"MSBuild and component selection","locale":"en"},"972":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-2","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"There are three distinct identifiers:","locale":"en"},"973":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-3","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Identifier","locale":"en"},"974":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-4","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Example","locale":"en"},"975":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-5","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"976":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-6","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Download ID","locale":"en"},"977":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-7","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"toolset `14.44.17.14`, SDK `26100`","locale":"en"},"978":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-8","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Identifier offered by the selected catalog","locale":"en"},"979":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-9","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Actual version","locale":"en"},"980":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-10","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"MSVC `14.44.35207`, SDK `10.0.26100.0`","locale":"en"},"981":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-11","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Directory version verified after extraction","locale":"en"},"982":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-12","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Directory key","locale":"en"},"983":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-13","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`vs2022-release/msvc-14.44.17.14_sdk-26100_host-x64_target-x64`","locale":"en"},"984":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-14","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Managed directory determined by source and download IDs","locale":"en"},"985":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-15","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Examples describe version syntax; availability depends on the selected catalog.","locale":"en"},"986":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-16","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`--vs-version` accepts `2022`/`17` and `2026`/`18`. `--channel` accepts `release`/`stable`\nand `preview`/`insiders`. A custom `--manifest` replaces both. The default is 2026 stable (`release`).\n`--arch HOST/TARGET` supports `x64/x64`, `x64/arm64`, `arm64/x64` and `arm64/arm64`.\nThe default follows the native Windows architecture, even when Hanamori itself runs under emulation.\nAn explicit `--arch` overrides project `host`/`target`; otherwise the project takes precedence over the native default.\nThe compiler host selects executable tools and MSBuild; the target selects CRT/SDK libraries and the MSBuild platform.\nAn ARM64-hosted compiler needs Windows 11 ARM64. ARM32 and ARM64EC are not supported.","locale":"en"},"987":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-17","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Different architecture pairs have separate directories and can coexist. For external directories with several pairs,\nuse `--dir PATH --arch HOST/TARGET` with `env`, `use`, `exec`, `import` or `doctor`.\nUnavailable catalog pairs fail explicitly; Hanamori does not substitute another architecture.","locale":"en"},"988":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-18","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`list-remote --all` groups toolsets and SDKs by VS 2022 and VS 2026, and expands the latest toolset’s packages in each group. It queries release channels by default. Add `--channel preview` (or `insiders`) to query both preview channels instead, without mixing release channels into the result. Identical IDs remain in their source groups. `--all` conflicts with `--vs-version`, `--manifest`, and `--toolset-id`. “All” covers versions still offered by the selected channels for the two supported VS generations, not every historical version Microsoft has ever published.","locale":"en"},"989":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-19","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`--all --json` returns `{ \"catalogs\": [...] }`. Each entry includes `vs_version`, `channel`, `manifest_url`, and the existing single-source fields `toolsets`, `sdks`, `selected_toolset_id`, and `packages`. A failure in either source fails the whole command without printing a partial list. The warning/strict manifest-integrity policy applies to both sources.","locale":"en"},"990":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-20","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`install [VERSION]` accepts an actual MSVC version or numeric prefix, or `latest`.\n`--sdk VERSION` accepts an actual four-part SDK version. `--no-sdk` excludes the SDK and, by default, MSBuild.\n`--toolset-id` and `--sdk-id` explicitly select catalog download IDs and conflict with\ncorresponding actual-version command-line arguments. Package metadata versions are not\nassumed to be compiler directory versions. Remote JSON reports unknown actual versions\nas `null`; it never fabricates a mapping.","locale":"en"},"991":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-21","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Without a version or project constraint, installation selects latest from the chosen catalog. The default reference is not an installation input. Actual versions are discovered from toolchain directories; if no reliable download-ID mapping exists, specify `--toolset-id` / `--sdk-id`. Project constraints are verified before publication.","locale":"en"},"992":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-22","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Managed installations without MSBuild live under `<toolchains-dir>/<source>/msvc-<download-id>_sdk-<download-id-or-none>_host-x64_target-x64`. The default MSBuild combination also has a `_msbuild-<version>` segment. The default base is `<manager>/toolchains`. Custom sources use a stable digest of the manifest URL, not the changing catalog contents. Local commands and completion honor the configured storage directory too.","locale":"en"},"993":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-23","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"A complete directory is reused after checking a small set of required files. An absent or incomplete managed directory is reinstalled at the same location; existing references keep working. `--reinstall` forces a fresh tree for other damaged files. `--name` creates or updates a reference after success.","locale":"en"},"994":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`--dir` installs a portable toolchain. A missing or empty destination is accepted. Replacing a nonempty external directory requires `--reinstall`, which replaces that entire directory; keep personal files elsewhere. Portable installations are discovered through an explicit `--dir` or an external reference. Uninstall does not delete external reference targets.","locale":"en"},"995":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"`--dry-run` may fetch catalog metadata but does not download payloads or create directories. Manifest checksum/size mismatches warn by default; `--strict-manifest-integrity` rejects them. Payload verification remains enabled. Each toolchain has its own SDK; the download cache shares payloads.","locale":"en"},"996":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-26","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation","content":"Installing an exact directory key fixes its source and download IDs. A custom-source key also requires its original `--manifest URL`. A project’s version constraints apply to version-based requests; an explicit key selects its own combination.","locale":"en"},"997":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-27","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"Installation includes MSVC, the Windows SDK and MSBuild by default, selecting MSBuild 18.x (VS 2026) or 17.x (VS 2022), C++ props/targets, task assemblies and FileTracker from the same catalog. `--no-msbuild` excludes MSBuild and keeps the compiler and SDK. `--no-sdk` or project `\"sdk\": null` defaults to a compiler-only installation.","locale":"en"},"998":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-28","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"Component selection follows explicit command-line options, then project settings, then defaults. Projects may set `\"msbuild\": true` or `false`; `--msbuild` / `--no-msbuild` override that setting. An explicit MSBuild requirement without the SDK fails; use `--no-msbuild` to cancel that requirement. Exact directory keys retain their component combination, so the new default does not add MSBuild to an existing key.","locale":"en"},"999":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-29","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"The supported scope is native C++ `.vcxproj` and `.sln` builds using VS 2026 v145 or VS 2022 v143. Use `--vs-version 2022` for v143 projects. Win32, ATL/MFC, C++/CLI, UWP, drivers, C# and IDE integration are outside that scope. Native Windows build acceptance remains pending; real downloads/extraction and Linux tests do not establish it.","locale":"en"},"1000":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-30","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"MSBuild combinations use `<source>/msvc-<ID>_sdk-<ID>_msbuild-<MSBuild version>_host-x64_target-x64`, independently of combinations without MSBuild. Reinstalling an exact key requires the catalog to still offer that MSBuild version; it never silently upgrades it. Retain a matching manifest and cache if upstream removes packages.","locale":"en"},"1001":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-31","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"The host needs the .NET Framework required by MSBuild. Installation extracts and checks files; on Windows, `doctor` also runs `MSBuild.exe -version` and reports runtime failures without installing system components. Invoke `MSBuild.exe` through the Hanamori environment so generated configuration selects the local compiler and SDK. Explicit conflicting project versions fail the build.","locale":"en"},"1002":{"id":"/en/docs/installation-32","page_id":"/en/docs/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/installation#msbuild-and-component-selection","content":"FileTracker uses the private directory instead of a system installation. Its upstream implementation has an ANSI-path restriction, so this initial version recommends an ASCII toolchain installation path such as `--dir D:/Tools/hanamori-build`. Unicode project directories are a separate case.","locale":"en"},"1003":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","type":"page","content":"Import, reinstall and remove","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/maintenance","locale":"en"},"1004":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-0","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance","content":"Manage directory discovery, references and reinstallation.","locale":"en"},"1005":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-1","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Reference external tools","locale":"en"},"1006":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-2","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reinstall-and-interrupted-operations","content":"Reinstall and interrupted operations","locale":"en"},"1007":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-3","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Import requires `--name`. It checks the selected combination and saves only its path and actual versions under the manager's `references/`. External files are untouched. Importing again updates that name: after moving an external directory, import its new path with the same name. Different combinations may have separate names.","locale":"en"},"1008":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-4","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Command","locale":"en"},"1009":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-5","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"1010":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-6","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"`remove NAME` / `unalias NAME`","locale":"en"},"1011":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-7","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Delete one reference; preserve files and other references","locale":"en"},"1012":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-8","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"`uninstall SELECTOR`","locale":"en"},"1013":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-9","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Delete a managed directory and references to it; reject external targets","locale":"en"},"1014":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-10","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"`cache clean`","locale":"en"},"1015":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-11","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Clean complete download cache entries without changing installations","locale":"en"},"1016":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-12","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"`self uninstall`","locale":"en"},"1017":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-13","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Remove the executable and its startup entries, preserving toolchains by default","locale":"en"},"1018":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-14","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"`self uninstall --purge`","locale":"en"},"1019":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-15","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Also clean managed tools, complete cache entries, config and references; preserve external tools","locale":"en"},"1020":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-16","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reference-external-tools","content":"Uninstall accepts a directory key, reference or unique version prefix. Missing payload files do not prevent removal. If the entire directory is gone, its exact key or dangling managed reference still allows cleanup. Deactivate a toolchain used by the current session first. On Windows, after acquiring the directory lock, uninstall uses Windows Restart Manager to close processes using the target files before deleting the directory. Toolchain cleanup during `self uninstall --purge` follows the same flow.","locale":"en"},"1021":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-17","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reinstall-and-interrupted-operations","content":"Rerun installation when a managed directory is absent, empty or missing required files. Use `--reinstall` for arbitrary damage beyond the small required-file check. These checks do not hash individual files.","locale":"en"},"1022":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-18","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reinstall-and-interrupted-operations","content":"Downloads, extraction and required-file checks finish before replacing an old managed tree. The new tree is staged on the destination volume. Publication renames the old tree aside and moves the new one into place, restoring the old tree on failure. The next installation for that target handles interrupted `.stage` / `.old` directories. Doctor reports issues without changing files.","locale":"en"},"1023":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-19","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reinstall-and-interrupted-operations","content":"Before replacing a directory on Windows, Hanamori registers the old installation's files with Windows Restart Manager, queries their users, logs process names and PIDs, and requests shutdown. Unresponsive processes are forcibly closed. Selection is scoped to the installation's files, rather than globally terminating processes named `MSBuild.exe`, `mspdbsrv.exe` or `vctip.exe`. The PDB server and telemetry program from the Microsoft packages remain installed.","locale":"en"},"1024":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-20","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reinstall-and-interrupted-operations","content":"Processes using the current installation are closed only after replacement contents have been extracted and validated; reuse and preparation failures leave those processes running. Cleanup of `.stage` / `.old` directories from an interrupted operation also closes processes using those leftover files. `--dry-run` never closes processes. Save work and finish related builds before reinstalling or uninstalling, as processes using the toolchain will be terminated. Processes that cannot be closed, directory handles or permissions can still block the operation; resolve the reported issue and retry. Shell deactivation does not stop resident processes.","locale":"en"},"1025":{"id":"/en/docs/maintenance-21","page_id":"/en/docs/maintenance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/maintenance#reinstall-and-interrupted-operations","content":"MSBuild combinations also check the engine, C++ targets, task assemblies, FileTracker and generated configuration. On Windows, doctor probes the engine version to distinguish runtime startup failures from missing files; other platforms only check files. Reinstall the full key from `list` to repair missing required components. Import preserves the MSBuild version of a Hanamori portable installation; it does not convert an arbitrary Visual Studio directory into a supported standalone MSBuild installation.","locale":"en"},"1026":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","type":"page","content":"PowerShell","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Shell integration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/powershell","locale":"en"},"1027":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell-0","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/powershell","content":"Choose the right 5.1/7 profile and pass scripts and arguments correctly.","locale":"en"},"1028":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell-1","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/powershell","content":"Load the current terminal first:","locale":"en"},"1029":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell-2","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/powershell","content":"Dot-sourcing lets the script modify this shell. Do not source an old output file after generation fails. Execution policy may restrict script loading; follow your system’s policy. Hanamori does not permanently relax it for you.","locale":"en"},"1030":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell-3","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/powershell","content":"For persistent setup, choose the runtime you actually use:","locale":"en"},"1031":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell-4","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/powershell","content":"Discovery queries that runtime’s user profile with profiles disabled. A discovery failure does not silently edit another runtime’s profile; use `--profile PATH` for an explicit file. Existing UTF-16 encoding is preserved.","locale":"en"},"1032":{"id":"/en/docs/powershell-5","page_id":"/en/docs/powershell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/powershell","content":"Through the wrapper, write the `exec` separator as `'--'`. Inspect `$LASTEXITCODE` for native child status. `shell deinit` affects future loads; restart the terminal to discard the already loaded function.","locale":"en"},"1033":{"id":"/en/docs/profiles","page_id":"/en/docs/profiles","type":"page","content":"Persistent startup profiles","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Shell integration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/profiles","locale":"en"},"1034":{"id":"/en/docs/profiles-0","page_id":"/en/docs/profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/profiles","content":"Install and remove dynamic startup loaders.","locale":"en"},"1035":{"id":"/en/docs/profiles-1","page_id":"/en/docs/profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/profiles","content":"`--use-on-cd` opts into project toolchain selection at startup and on directory changes.\nKeep this flag when updating initialization; omitting it disables tracking on subsequent\nloads. In PowerShell, place initialization after prompt theme setup. See\nShell integration for behavior and shell differences.","locale":"en"},"1036":{"id":"/en/docs/profiles-2","page_id":"/en/docs/profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/profiles","content":"`--completions` opts into generating fresh completion with the hook on every startup.\nKeep it when updating initialization; omitting it restores hook-only loading. In Zsh,\nplace the managed block after `compinit` or your framework's completion setup.\nDeinit and self uninstall clean the whole block using existing ownership records;\nrestart the shell to remove completion already loaded in memory.\nSee terminal completion.","locale":"en"},"1037":{"id":"/en/docs/profiles-3","page_id":"/en/docs/profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/profiles","content":"`--profile PATH` selects a specific startup file; `--shell-executable` selects the\nruntime used for profile discovery. With automatic detection, discovery uses the detected\nexecutable, so PowerShell 7 selects its own profile rather than Windows PowerShell 5.1's.\nIf `--shell` is omitted, a recognizable `--shell-executable` name also selects the shell\ntype; explicit `--shell` takes precedence. An explicit `--profile` overrides profile\ndiscovery. For renamed runtimes, specify `--shell` and `--shell-executable` together.\nInitialization stores a loader that calls\n`env`, not a fixed toolchain snapshot. Managed blocks preserve surrounding bytes, encoding\nand newline style. Repeated init/deinit is stable. Bash setup maintains the interactive\nentry and an appropriate login-profile bridge; Zsh respects `ZDOTDIR`. Deinit affects\nfuture sessions and does not deactivate an open terminal.","locale":"en"},"1038":{"id":"/en/docs/profiles-4","page_id":"/en/docs/profiles","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/profiles","content":"Startup loaders do not store a manager directory. Set `HANAMORI_HOME` in your profile to persist a custom location.","locale":"en"},"1039":{"id":"/en/docs/projects","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","type":"page","content":"Project selection","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Toolchains and execution"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/projects","locale":"en"},"1040":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-0","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Pin project requirements and understand local resolution.","locale":"en"},"1041":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-1","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Put `hanamori-toolchain.json` in the project root:","locale":"en"},"1042":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-2","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Field","locale":"en"},"1043":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-3","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"1044":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-4","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`toolset`","locale":"en"},"1045":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-5","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Required actual MSVC version or numeric prefix with one to three segments","locale":"en"},"1046":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-6","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`sdk`","locale":"en"},"1047":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-7","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Actual four-part version; `null` means no SDK; omitted means unconstrained","locale":"en"},"1048":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-8","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`msbuild`","locale":"en"},"1049":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-9","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Optional boolean: `true` requires MSBuild, `false` excludes it; omitted leaves local selection unconstrained; installation enables it by default with the SDK, or disables it when SDK is `null`","locale":"en"},"1050":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-10","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`host`, `target`","locale":"en"},"1051":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-11","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Optional `x64` or `arm64`; host defaults to native Windows architecture, target defaults to host","locale":"en"},"1052":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-12","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`vs`, `channel`","locale":"en"},"1053":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-13","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Optional source constraints; source-unknown imports cannot satisfy them","locale":"en"},"1054":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-14","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`schema_version`","locale":"en"},"1055":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-15","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Optional, currently `1`","locale":"en"},"1056":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-16","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Unknown fields are ignored. The nearest file in the current directory or its ancestors\nwins. A malformed nearest file stops selection rather than falling through to a parent\nor the default. Selection priority is explicit selector/directory, then project, then\n`default`. Missing matches fail; several matches list candidates and require a directory key or\nalias. A numeric prefix does not silently pick one SDK or source over another.","locale":"en"},"1057":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-17","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"`install` also reads the nearest project. Explicit actual-version/SDK options replace\nthe corresponding project constraint; omitted fields retain it. Explicit download IDs\nsupply payload selection and still must satisfy retained actual-version constraints.\nFor example, a project that pins real versions can be installed using catalog IDs:","locale":"en"},"1058":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-18","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"A project file describes a combination, not a promise that upstream will host its\npayloads forever. Keep the original install command, download IDs and cached payloads when needed. An explicit managed directory key selects its own combination without reading the project.","locale":"en"},"1059":{"id":"/en/docs/projects-19","page_id":"/en/docs/projects","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/projects","content":"Reference names contain 1–64 ASCII letters, digits, hyphens or underscores, excluding command names. `default` is the special allowed alias. Removing an absent alias is harmless.","locale":"en"},"1060":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"page","content":"First compilation","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start","locale":"en"},"1061":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-0","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start","content":"Install a toolchain, compile a complete C++ example and run it.","locale":"en"},"1062":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-1","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#1-install-a-toolchain","content":"1\\. Install a toolchain","locale":"en"},"1063":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-2","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#2-save-the-source","content":"2\\. Save the source","locale":"en"},"1064":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-3","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#3-build-and-run","content":"3\\. Build and run","locale":"en"},"1065":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-4","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#4-activate-this-terminal","content":"4\\. Activate this terminal","locale":"en"},"1066":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-5","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#5-optional-cleanup","content":"5\\. Optional cleanup","locale":"en"},"1067":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-6","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start","content":"Get Hanamori, add its executable directory to PATH, and open PowerShell in a writable project directory. These commands use the default VS 2026 stable catalog. Installation needs network access and disk space.","locale":"en"},"1068":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-7","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#1-install-a-toolchain","content":"`stable` is a local alias you create. Installation does not activate this terminal, and `default` only records a selection. Available versions depend on the chosen catalog.","locale":"en"},"1069":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-8","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#2-save-the-source","content":"Create `hello.cpp`:","locale":"en"},"1070":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-9","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#2-save-the-source","content":"The example uses both the C++ standard library and Windows SDK. Do not install with `--no-sdk` for this example.","locale":"en"},"1071":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-10","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#3-build-and-run","content":"`exec` needs no shell initialization: only the child receives the compiler environment. Quoting `'--'` in PowerShell also works through an initialized Hanamori wrapper. Expect `Hello from Hanamori!` and a process ID that may change each run.","locale":"en"},"1072":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-11","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#4-activate-this-terminal","content":"`use` selects from the nearest project file, then the default. A `hanamori-toolchain.json` overrides the default; `hanamori use stable` explicitly overrides project selection. `deactivate` restores the original environment. To load the hook in new terminals, see startup profiles.","locale":"en"},"1073":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-12","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#5-optional-cleanup","content":"This removes the whole managed installation and its aliases, not `hello.cpp` in your project. Do not store personal files inside toolchain directories. To delete only the stable name, use `remove stable`; the managed directory remains discoverable by list. See maintenance.","locale":"en"},"1074":{"id":"/en/docs/release","page_id":"/en/docs/release","type":"page","content":"Release process","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/release","locale":"en"},"1075":{"id":"/en/docs/release-0","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release","content":"Select an existing tag, share checks, and publish Windows assets and the crate.","locale":"en"},"1076":{"id":"/en/docs/release-1","page_id":"/en/docs/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/release#prepare-a-version-and-tag","content":"Prepare a version and tag","locale":"en"},"1077":{"id":"/en/docs/release-2","page_id":"/en/docs/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"Select a tag and channel","locale":"en"},"1078":{"id":"/en/docs/release-3","page_id":"/en/docs/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"Checks, builds and publication","locale":"en"},"1079":{"id":"/en/docs/release-4","page_id":"/en/docs/release","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/release#cratesio-credentials-and-retries","content":"crates.io credentials and retries","locale":"en"},"1080":{"id":"/en/docs/release-5","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release","content":"The Release workflow publishes both GitHub Release assets and the `hanamori` crate. Pushing a `v*` tag publishes to both channels. Manual runs let you choose a tag and a channel. Ordinary main pushes and website builds do not publish versions.","locale":"en"},"1081":{"id":"/en/docs/release-6","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#prepare-a-version-and-tag","content":"Use the repository's `xtask` commands from the workspace or one of its packages:","locale":"en"},"1082":{"id":"/en/docs/release-7","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#prepare-a-version-and-tag","content":"Choose one bump command. It updates `workspace.package.version` in `Cargo.toml` and uses\nCargo to regenerate the workspace entries in `Cargo.lock`, preserving locked dependency\nversions. It does not commit changes or create tags. Commit the version change before tagging:","locale":"en"},"1083":{"id":"/en/docs/release-8","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#prepare-a-version-and-tag","content":"`cargo xtask tag` creates an annotated `vVERSION` tag at `HEAD` without pushing. The default\nis the current workspace version, not the highest existing Git tag. An explicit version is\nalso supported, for example `cargo xtask tag 0.1.2 --push`; it must match the workspace version.\nTracked changes must be committed, and an existing tag is never replaced.","locale":"en"},"1084":{"id":"/en/docs/release-9","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#prepare-a-version-and-tag","content":"`--push` pushes only the created tag to `origin`, triggering both release channels. If the\npush fails, the local tag is retained and the command prints the `git push` command to retry.","locale":"en"},"1085":{"id":"/en/docs/release-10","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"In Actions, choose **Release → Run workflow** and use the workflow on `main`:","locale":"en"},"1086":{"id":"/en/docs/release-11","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"Input","locale":"en"},"1087":{"id":"/en/docs/release-12","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"1088":{"id":"/en/docs/release-13","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"`tag`","locale":"en"},"1089":{"id":"/en/docs/release-14","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"An optional existing `v*` Git tag, such as `v0.1.0`. If omitted, the highest `v*` tag in Git version order is selected, independently of tag creation dates or GitHub Release dates.","locale":"en"},"1090":{"id":"/en/docs/release-15","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"`target`","locale":"en"},"1091":{"id":"/en/docs/release-16","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"`all` (default) publishes both channels; `github` publishes only GitHub Release assets; `crates-io` publishes only the crate.","locale":"en"},"1092":{"id":"/en/docs/release-17","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#select-a-tag-and-channel","content":"The workflow does not create tags. Publication stops if there is no `v*` tag, the requested tag does not exist, or the tag version differs from the Cargo version in its source. A tag push selects that tag; an explicit manual `tag` input takes precedence.","locale":"en"},"1093":{"id":"/en/docs/release-18","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"Update the workspace version and Cargo-generated lockfile, then create a `v*` tag pointing to the intended source.","locale":"en"},"1094":{"id":"/en/docs/release-19","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"Release fetches all tags, resolves the selected commit, and verifies its Cargo package name, version and binary target.","locale":"en"},"1095":{"id":"/en/docs/release-20","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"The reusable CI workflow and Installers workflow check Rust code and installer scripts separately at the same commit. Rust checks include formatting, module architecture and tests; installer checks cover arguments and metadata on Linux and native installation on Windows. Windows uses the release profile and `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` / `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` target.","locale":"en"},"1096":{"id":"/en/docs/release-21","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"After checks pass, the selected channels build and publish from the same commit. Ordinary branch CI does not respond to tag pushes; the two channels in one Release run share checks instead of running `cargo test` separately.","locale":"en"},"1097":{"id":"/en/docs/release-22","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"The GitHub channel builds on Windows x64 and `windows-11-arm`, packaging `hanamori-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe`, `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` and matching ZIPs containing `hanamori.exe`. All four published asset SHA-256 digests are verified.","locale":"en"},"1098":{"id":"/en/docs/release-23","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"The crates.io channel runs `cargo publish --locked`, retaining Cargo's compilation check of the packaged source. Only `hanamori` is published, not `hanamori-test-support` or `xtask`.","locale":"en"},"1099":{"id":"/en/docs/release-24","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"The two channels run independently after shared checks pass. If one fails, retry only the unpublished channel with the same tag. When manually publishing an older tag, checks and builds use that tag's source, not the main source that defines the workflow.","locale":"en"},"1100":{"id":"/en/docs/release-25","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#checks-builds-and-publication","content":"A passing CI run, website deployment or successful publication to one channel does not prove publication to the other. After a GitHub Release, also verify that users can download its assets. The download page and self-update use the asset names above; the page queries the public API without a token.","locale":"en"},"1101":{"id":"/en/docs/release-26","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#cratesio-credentials-and-retries","content":"Configure `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` in the repository's Actions Secrets with a crates.io API token authorized to publish `hanamori`. The first publication requires permission to create the crate; subsequent publications require permission to publish that crate.","locale":"en"},"1102":{"id":"/en/docs/release-27","page_id":"/en/docs/release","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/release#cratesio-credentials-and-retries","content":"Run `cargo publish --locked --registry crates-io -p hanamori --dry-run` locally to compile the packaged source without uploading. A version already on crates.io cannot be overwritten. If the crate is already published and only GitHub assets are missing, select `target=github`.","locale":"en"},"1103":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","type":"page","content":"Uninstall Hanamori","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","locale":"en"},"1104":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-0","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"Remove this executable, or purge the selected manager’s owned data.","locale":"en"},"1105":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-1","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"To uninstall Hanamori itself:","locale":"en"},"1106":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-2","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"On Windows, the installer records only the user PATH entry it added in the adjacent\n`hanamori.exe.install.json`. Self uninstall removes that entry and receipt, preserving\nother PATH entries and environment-variable references. Entries that existed before\ninstallation remain user-owned. Moving the executable requires manually cleaning the\noriginal installation's PATH entry.","locale":"en"},"1107":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-3","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"The default removes the running executable, its `.outdated` upgrade backup, and recorded\nstartup entries belonging to that executable. MSVC, SDKs, configuration and named references\nremain available for a later installation of Hanamori. The executable's parent directory\nis never recursively deleted: a portable copy in Downloads does not give Hanamori ownership\nof Downloads.","locale":"en"},"1108":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-4","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"`--purge` removes discovered managed toolchain directories under the configured `toolchains_dir`, including incomplete trees. It cleans complete payloads from the configured cache and deletes named references and `config.json`. External imports and directories created by `install --dir` lose their references but keep their files. Managers configured to share the same toolchain storage also share these physical directories, so removal affects them all. A managed directory is removed in full; keep unrelated files elsewhere. Move the executable or manager outside a managed toolchain before purging it. Unknown files, partial download workspaces, profile backups and lock files\n(including `.update.lock`) are retained; remaining directories are not recursively erased.\nA shared cache may lose complete payloads, as with `cache clean`.","locale":"en"},"1109":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-5","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"Deactivate the current session first and close other terminals using Hanamori. Toolchain\nor cache cleanup failures stop before deleting the program and remaining manager metadata.\nEarlier completed removals are not rolled back. `--purge` reuses the file usage handling from toolchain uninstall and cache cleanup. Resolve the reported error before retrying. Incomplete managed directories can still be uninstalled. A dry run performs no writes, registry edits, lock acquisition, process shutdown or helper launch.","locale":"en"},"1110":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-6","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"`shell init` records the executable, selected runtime when available, actual profile\nlocations and owned content in the user data directory's `Hanamori/shell/registrations`\ndirectory (`LOCALAPPDATA` on Windows; `XDG_DATA_HOME` or `~/.local/share` on Unix). Bash login\nbridges and CMD helper bundles are included. Self uninstall checks the recorded profile block\nor CMD loader ownership before removal and preserves modified entries with a notice. Entries\nwithout ownership records must be removed manually, or registered by\nrerunning `shell init` with the same profile/runtime options first. Manually configured PATH\nentries and Windows uninstall registry entries are not modified. Restart the shell afterward\nto discard its already loaded hook.","locale":"en"},"1111":{"id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall-7","page_id":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/self-uninstall","content":"On Windows, a temporary PowerShell script waits for the parent process to exit, then deletes\nthe exact executable and backup paths. The CLI reports **scheduled**, not completed, removal;\nthe helper reports its result separately. It never kills other processes. If deletion fails,\nit retains `failure.txt`, `files.json` and `uninstall.ps1` in the displayed temporary directory.\nClose processes holding the files and rerun `uninstall.ps1` without arguments. Successful\ncleanup deletes the helper's own files and empty temporary directory.","locale":"en"},"1112":{"id":"/en/docs/shell","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","type":"page","content":"Shell integration","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Shell integration"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shell","locale":"en"},"1113":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-0","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell","content":"Initialize, activate and restore a terminal environment.","locale":"en"},"1114":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-1","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shell#automatic-project-switching","content":"Automatic project switching","locale":"en"},"1115":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-2","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"Shell detection","locale":"en"},"1116":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-3","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell","content":"Add `--completions` to `hanamori env` to register Tab completion with the hook. This is opt-in and supports PowerShell, Bash and Zsh; Zsh requires `compinit` first. Standalone `hanamori completions` is also available. See terminal completion.","locale":"en"},"1117":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-4","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell","content":"Initialize once in each shell. By default, initialization only loads the hook; it does not\nselect an installation, inspect a project, or access the network. `--auto-activate` calls\n`use` once when loading into an inactive session; failure leaves the terminal usable.\nOpt into `--use-on-cd` to follow project toolchains as the working directory changes.","locale":"en"},"1118":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-5","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#automatic-project-switching","content":"Choose the command for your shell and reopen it. Temporary hooks also accept `env --use-on-cd`.\nThis includes initial selection at startup, so `--auto-activate` is unnecessary. It conflicts\nwith `--dir`, which binds a fixed toolchain directory.","locale":"en"},"1119":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-6","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#automatic-project-switching","content":"On directory changes, the nearest `hanamori-toolchain.json` in the current directory or its\nancestors wins. Nested projects override their parents. Outside a project, the default\ntoolchain is selected; without either a project or a default, the current environment stays\nunchanged. Invalid configuration, ambiguous matches and missing toolchains report errors\nwithout replacing the environment or downloading tools. An unchanged target produces no\nenvironment updates or repeated notices.","locale":"en"},"1120":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-7","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#automatic-project-switching","content":"Zsh switches immediately on directory changes. Bash and PowerShell check when returning to\nthe prompt: `cd project; build` does not switch before `build` on the same line. Use\n`hanamori exec` / `hanamori run` for scripts and chained commands. PowerShell handles only\nfilesystem locations; place initialization after prompt theme setup.","locale":"en"},"1121":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-8","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#automatic-project-switching","content":"Manual `use` and `deactivate` remain effective until the next directory change. Reloading\ndoes not duplicate callbacks; loading a hook without `--use-on-cd` disables tracking while\nkeeping the active environment. Editing a project file without changing directories does\nnot refresh automatically; run `hanamori use`. See CMD integration for its limits.","locale":"en"},"1122":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-9","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"`env` and `shell init/activate/deactivate/deinit` detect the calling shell when `--shell`\nis omitted. Detection walks up to 16 parent processes, supporting Bash, Zsh, PowerShell\nand CMD. It does not use `$SHELL` or `COMSPEC`, which may describe a different shell.\nAn explicit `--shell` wins; if detection fails, the command asks you to specify it.\nThe generated hooks keep passing an explicit shell for subsequent `use`/`deactivate`.","locale":"en"},"1123":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-10","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"On Windows, Bash/Zsh hooks and profile loaders use the current MSYS runtime's `cygpath`\nto translate Hanamori's native executable path before invoking it. Keep `cygpath` on\nPATH. After upgrading from a build that embedded an unconverted Windows path, regenerate\nand apply `env`; if you installed a startup entry, rerun `shell init` with the executable\ndirectly to replace that loader as well.","locale":"en"},"1124":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-11","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"PowerShell:","locale":"en"},"1125":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-12","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"Bash and Zsh:","locale":"en"},"1126":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-13","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"Each command selects its manager through `--manager-dir`, then `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform default (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori` on Windows). A generation-time `--manager-dir` does not pin future commands. Set `HANAMORI_HOME` in your startup configuration to persist a custom manager directory. An explicit `env --dir PATH` supplies a toolchain directory default for calls without an explicit selector; it does not register that directory.","locale":"en"},"1127":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-14","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"`use`, `exec --using` and `shell activate` share local selection. For a direct,\nunregistered directory, use `--dir`, and supply `--toolset`/`--sdk` or `--no-sdk` if\nits contents are ambiguous. These versions are actual directory versions.","locale":"en"},"1128":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-15","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"Source these one-time scripts in the calling shell. For `KEY=VALUE` inspection, use\n`hanamori shell activate stable --plain`. This skips shell detection and cannot be\ncombined with `--shell` or `--output`; its output is not an activation script.\nFailed generation does not replace an existing output file. Calling `use` without\nintegration explains how to initialize; a child process cannot modify its parent shell.","locale":"en"},"1129":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-16","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"Activation preserves the original managed-variable baseline. Switching A → B does not\naccumulate compiler paths; `deactivate` restores the pre-A values. Empty and unset values\nremain distinct where the shell supports them. Switching to compiler-only clears injected\nSDK values. Unrelated environment variables remain intact. Independent terminals can use\ndifferent combinations. `current` reads the active session snapshot rather than resolving\nthe default or project again. `current` and deactivation remain usable with a\nbroken global configuration or missing installation.","locale":"en"},"1130":{"id":"/en/docs/shell-17","page_id":"/en/docs/shell","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/shell#shell-detection","content":"`exec --using SELECTOR -- COMMAND [ARGS...]` works in a clean terminal, forwards literal\narguments, inherits streams and preserves the child exit status. Use `--` to separate\nchild options from manager options. It executes argv, not a shell expression: pipes,\nredirection, expansion and builtins require an explicit shell command. In a loaded PowerShell function, quote the separator as `'--'`. Windows PowerShell\nuses the existing encoded argv launcher to preserve empty strings and quotes.","locale":"en"},"1131":{"id":"/en/docs/support","page_id":"/en/docs/support","type":"page","content":"Platform support","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Get started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/support","locale":"en"},"1132":{"id":"/en/docs/support-0","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Distinguish program builds, shell integration and native MSVC execution.","locale":"en"},"1133":{"id":"/en/docs/support-1","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Area","locale":"en"},"1134":{"id":"/en/docs/support-2","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Current scope","locale":"en"},"1135":{"id":"/en/docs/support-3","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Native compilation","locale":"en"},"1136":{"id":"/en/docs/support-4","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Windows x64 / ARM64 hosts; x64 and ARM64 targets","locale":"en"},"1137":{"id":"/en/docs/support-5","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Distribution and self-update","locale":"en"},"1138":{"id":"/en/docs/support-6","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"`x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` / `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, EXE and ZIP","locale":"en"},"1139":{"id":"/en/docs/support-7","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Shells","locale":"en"},"1140":{"id":"/en/docs/support-8","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"PowerShell 5.1/7, Bash, Zsh; CMD is experimental","locale":"en"},"1141":{"id":"/en/docs/support-9","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"POSIX shells on Windows","locale":"en"},"1142":{"id":"/en/docs/support-10","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"MSYS path conversion requires the current runtime’s `cygpath`","locale":"en"},"1143":{"id":"/en/docs/support-11","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Linux/other Unix","locale":"en"},"1144":{"id":"/en/docs/support-12","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Source development and some logic/shell tests, not native MSVC execution","locale":"en"},"1145":{"id":"/en/docs/support-13","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Combinations","locale":"en"},"1146":{"id":"/en/docs/support-14","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Independent MSVC/SDK directories; compiler-only supported; no sharing of installed SDK files","locale":"en"},"1147":{"id":"/en/docs/support-15","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"The CLI provides the `run` execution alias, the `completions` command and optional `--use-on-cd` project switching. There is currently no GUI, ARM32/ARM64EC target or cross-manager reference ledger. Loading a hook does not activate by default. Explicit `--auto-activate` attempts activation once in an inactive session; `--use-on-cd` also reselects on directory changes. See Shell integration for shell-specific triggers.","locale":"en"},"1148":{"id":"/en/docs/support-16","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"Local tests, cross-compilation and native Windows acceptance are different evidence. See testing and native acceptance for the verification procedure. A successful build does not establish acceptance for every shell or real compiler combination.","locale":"en"},"1149":{"id":"/en/docs/support-17","page_id":"/en/docs/support","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/support","content":"ARM64-hosted tools require Windows 11 ARM64. Microsoft introduced native ARM64 Visual Studio tools in VS 2022 17.4; see Visual Studio on Arm devices. Hanamori selects the host compiler and target libraries independently.","locale":"en"},"1150":{"id":"/en/docs/testing","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","type":"page","content":"Testing and native acceptance","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/testing","locale":"en"},"1151":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-0","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Run local checks and understand the limits of synthetic tests.","locale":"en"},"1152":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-1","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/testing#native-msbuild-acceptance","content":"Native MSBuild acceptance","locale":"en"},"1153":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-2","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/testing#architecture-acceptance","content":"Architecture acceptance","locale":"en"},"1154":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-3","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Run `cargo test --locked -p hanamori --test cli completions::` for completion coverage:\nreal Bash candidates, Zsh's Tab completion in a line editor, PowerShell `CompleteInput`,\nstandalone scripts, hooks, profiles, repeated loading, hidden commands and `exec --`.\nWindows also runs PowerShell 5.1. Bash/Zsh lookup checks the executable override, then PATH;\nBash also checks the Git installation found on PATH and `ProgramFiles/Git/bin/bash.exe`.\nOverride runtimes with `HANAMORI_TEST_BASH` / `HANAMORI_TEST_ZSH`.\nUnavailable Windows Zsh is explicitly skipped unless an override requires it.\nRerun generation and actual-shell cases when upgrading `clap_complete`.","locale":"en"},"1155":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-4","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"`cargo test --locked -p hanamori --test cli completions::dynamic::` uses real directories and imported references\nto check selectors, ambiguous versions, manager precedence, direct directory selection,\nisolated broken references and read-only behavior. The shell suite also covers dynamic candidates,\nquoted paths, equals-form options, HOME changes and exit-code preservation in Bash\nReadline, Zsh's line editor and PowerShell.","locale":"en"},"1156":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-5","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Dynamic parsing uses a pinned `clap_complete` Rust engine; its `unstable-dynamic` feature\nis not exposed as a public shell protocol. The internal `shell complete` command only\nqueries candidates. Shell adapter templates live in `src/commands/completions/`, while\nstatic command completion still comes from the same Clap tree. Check both template\nadaptation and dynamic parsing when upgrading; do not edit generated scripts manually.","locale":"en"},"1157":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-6","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"CI uses the existing Linux and Windows workflow. Tests use real implementation paths,\nlocal HTTP servers, synthetic archives and real available shells. Required-shell mode\nprevents silently treating missing shells as successful integration coverage.","locale":"en"},"1158":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-7","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"For main pushes and pull requests, Rust CI runs only when Rust source, Rust tests, workspace\npackages, Cargo/toolchain configuration or related release automation change. The Installers\nworkflow checks the root installer scripts and `tests/installers/`; Rust source and build\nconfiguration changes also trigger installer integration checks. Website checks `site/` and\nrebuilds distributed installer files when the scripts change. README-only, website-only and\ninstaller-only changes skip Rust CI. Release calls Rust CI and Installers with the same source\ncommit and requires both to pass before publishing, regardless of changed-path filters.","locale":"en"},"1159":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-8","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"For ordinary local checks, run `cargo test --workspace`. Unavailable optional shells are\nreported as skipped; an explicitly configured runtime must exist. Windows Bash/Zsh tests\nneed Git Bash or MSYS2 with `cygpath`, rather than WSL. Test subprocesses retain a usable\nWindows temporary directory while isolating Hanamori state and configuration. CMD lifecycle\nfixtures use a small system PATH so the developer's installed tools do not consume the\nbatch command length limit.","locale":"en"},"1160":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-9","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Installer tests run through `tests/installers/run.mjs`, using only Node built-in modules,\nwithout website dependencies. The portable suite needs Node, Bash and PowerShell 7, but\ndoes not need Cargo or a Hanamori executable. It checks arguments, platform rejection,\nrelease metadata, architecture selection and preservation after a corrupt download:","locale":"en"},"1161":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-10","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"The Windows suite accepts a real built EXE; the test runner never invokes Cargo itself.\nFor a native x64 host:","locale":"en"},"1162":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-11","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"On native ARM64, replace the build target, executable path and test target with\n`aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`. Version, size and SHA-256 come from the supplied executable.\nLocal HTTP fixtures serve releases and downloads; profiles and registry keys are isolated.\nPowerShell 5.1/7 cover first and repeated installation, Unicode paths, PATH preservation,\nskip options and retaining the old executable after download, digest, size or version failures.\nGit Bash and MSYS2 each cover piped installation, both path formats, repeat installation,\nfailure preservation, skip options and hook loading in a fresh Bash session.","locale":"en"},"1163":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-12","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Override installer runtimes with `HANAMORI_TEST_POWERSHELL`, `HANAMORI_TEST_PWSH` and\n`HANAMORI_TEST_BASH`. Bash also checks PATH, the Git installation found on PATH and the\ndefault Git installation. Additional MSYS2 uses `HANAMORI_TEST_MSYS2_BASH` or\n`msys64/usr/bin/bash.exe` on the system drive. Without `--require-shells`, unavailable\ndefault runtimes are reported as skipped; explicit missing runtimes always fail, as does\nan entirely skipped run. `--require-shells` requires all primary shells for the suite;\nadditional MSYS2 may still be skipped unless explicitly configured. Windows CI explicitly\nselects Git Bash; x64 also requires MSYS2, while ARM64 checks additional MSYS2 when available.","locale":"en"},"1164":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-13","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"`cargo test --workspace` does not execute root installer tests. Toolchain installation,\nself-uninstall, shell integration and completions remain Rust tests. Library tests still\ncover receipt-based PATH cleanup without editing the user's real PATH. Website build,\ntype checking and tests remain independent; see Website maintenance.","locale":"en"},"1165":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-14","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Run `cargo test --locked -p hanamori --lib --test api` for\nextraction, publication and directory discovery coverage. The CAB regression uses a real MSZIP\narchive and decoder, counting underlying bytes read to catch per-file decompression\nrestarts. It also covers multiple folders, skipped ranges, empty files, corrupt checksums\nand missing files. SDK tests check staging location, failure cleanup and actual file\nprogress; transaction tests check successful replacement, preservation on failed preparation and restoration after interrupted publication. The install CLI suite also removes complete trees, cl.exe, SDK libraries and Windows Kits before reinstalling, exercises `--reinstall` for other missing files, and verifies explicit external replacement and preservation on failure.","locale":"en"},"1166":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-15","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"Synthetic archive read counts show repeated work, not native Windows installation timing.\nFor real performance measurements, record versions, storage, cache state and separate\ndownload/extraction durations, then verify that the resulting toolchain works.","locale":"en"},"1167":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-16","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"For actual compiler acceptance, install or import two real MSVC/SDK combinations on native\nWindows. Both compiler and SDK directory versions must differ. Use managed directory keys from `list` or named references:","locale":"en"},"1168":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-17","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing","content":"This ignored gate runs in the sequence A → B (inheriting A) → A from an isolated environment.\nIt invokes `rc.exe` by name to compile resources, compiles and links C++ using Windows/standard\nheaders, the static CRT and SDK libraries, then invokes `mt.exe` by name to embed a manifest.\nThe built program checks the resource and embedded manifest contents. The gate also checks\ndistinct/stable compiler fingerprints and unchanged reference contents, using paths with spaces and Unicode.\nIt downloads or deletes no tools. Missing inputs or a non-Windows host fail explicitly.\nCross-compilation, Linux synthetic tests and Wine do not establish native acceptance.\nInteractive PowerShell 5.1/7, Git Bash/Zsh, CMD/AutoRun, independent terminals, cross-volume\noperations and preservation when files are occupied must each be verified with their results recorded.","locale":"en"},"1169":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-18","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#native-msbuild-acceptance","content":"`cargo test --locked -p hanamori --test cli install::msbuild` covers VS 2022/2026 extraction paths using synthetic VSIX/MSI/CAB files, private FileTracker placement, independent combinations, project requirements, missing-file repair, rollback and MSBuild → ordinary → MSBuild environment restoration. Those archives contain no executable MSBuild.","locale":"en"},"1170":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-19","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#native-msbuild-acceptance","content":"On Windows x64 / ARM64 without Visual Studio/Build Tools, install A with `--vs-version 2022` and B with the default VS 2026, using different compiler/SDK versions and the default components (including MSBuild), set the same three environment variables, then run:","locale":"en"},"1171":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-20","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#native-msbuild-acceptance","content":"The gate selects v143/v145 for each toolchain and builds `.vcxproj` and `.sln` files referencing a static-library project in A → B (inheriting A) → A order. It exercises Debug/Release, resources, manifests, incremental compilation, changed-library relinking, Clean/Rebuild and evaluated compiler/SDK/targets paths inside the selected installation. An explicitly unavailable SDK must fail. Builds disable node reuse; binary logs reside in the temporary build directory.","locale":"en"},"1172":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-21","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#native-msbuild-acceptance","content":"Repeat on a host with another Visual Studio installation to check independence, and run the installation guide's build commands from PowerShell and Git Bash/MSYS2. MSBuild examples use `-p:` and `-t:`. If MSYS2 rewrites `cl`'s `/link`, use per-command `MSYS2_ARG_CONV_EXCL='*' cl ...`; installing MSBuild does not address argument conversion. These native checks remain pending; current Linux evidence covers download/extraction and automated regressions only.","locale":"en"},"1173":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-22","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#architecture-acceptance","content":"CI runs on Linux, native Windows x64 and `windows-11-arm`. Archive tests cover all four host/target pairs for VS 2022 and VS 2026, including MSBuild, independent directory identities and required-file checks.","locale":"en"},"1174":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-23","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#architecture-acceptance","content":"Install each pair on a compatible compiler host, set `HANAMORI_TEST_MANAGER_DIR` and `HANAMORI_TEST_TOOLCHAIN_A` to that installation, then run:","locale":"en"},"1175":{"id":"/en/docs/testing-24","page_id":"/en/docs/testing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/testing#architecture-acceptance","content":"This gate compiles and links C/C++ with the actual compiler and builds a `.vcxproj` with MSBuild. It checks PE Machine (`0x8664` or `0xaa64`) and executes the result when the OS supports its target. Run x64/arm64 on x64 Windows; run arm64/arm64, arm64/x64 and x64/arm64 on Windows 11 ARM64. The two-toolchain gates also accept ARM64 installations and use their selected MSBuild platform. Real Windows acceptance remains separate from Linux extraction checks.","locale":"en"},"1176":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"1177":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Choose diagnostics and recovery steps based on the actual failure.","locale":"en"},"1178":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Symptom","locale":"en"},"1179":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Next steps","locale":"en"},"1180":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Tab offers no candidates","locale":"en"},"1181":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Load the completion script, or run `shell init --completions` and reopen the terminal; see terminal completion","locale":"en"},"1182":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Zsh asks for compinit","locale":"en"},"1183":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Place the Hanamori block after framework/compinit initialization, then reload it; the toolchain hook remains usable","locale":"en"},"1184":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Missing local versions or aliases","locale":"en"},"1185":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Check --manager-dir / HANAMORI_HOME / platform defaults and check toolchains_dir and inspect directories/references with list or doctor; shared, ambiguous versions are not suggested","locale":"en"},"1186":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"PowerShell does not complete fixed values such as channel","locale":"en"},"1187":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Local dynamic candidates are supported; fixed enums and ordinary paths retain static-generator limitations","locale":"en"},"1188":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"`hanamori` not found","locale":"en"},"1189":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Invoke the EXE directly; inspect PATH; reopen the terminal after persistent changes","locale":"en"},"1190":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"`use` says integration is missing","locale":"en"},"1191":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Successfully generate and source `env`, or use hook-free `exec`","locale":"en"},"1192":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Shell detection fails","locale":"en"},"1193":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Pass `--shell powershell/bash/zsh/cmd`; changing `$SHELL` or COMSPEC is not a fix","locale":"en"},"1194":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Windows Zsh reports `D:\\…` command not found","locale":"en"},"1195":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Invoke the new EXE directly, check `cygpath`, reload env / rerun shell init","locale":"en"},"1196":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Wrong PowerShell profile","locale":"en"},"1197":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Choose `--shell-executable pwsh` or `powershell.exe`, or use `--profile`","locale":"en"},"1198":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Ambiguous version prefix","locale":"en"},"1199":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Inspect `list --json` and use an exact managed directory key or fixed alias","locale":"en"},"1200":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Cannot map actual version to download ID","locale":"en"},"1201":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Query `list-remote`, then specify `--toolset-id` / `--sdk-id` while retaining project constraints","locale":"en"},"1202":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Malformed nearest project file","locale":"en"},"1203":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Fix it; it is not skipped in favor of a parent/default","locale":"en"},"1204":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Download failure","locale":"en"},"1205":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Inspect the reported URL, proxy and network; distinguish cache from workspace","locale":"en"},"1206":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Deleted files prevent use","locale":"en"},"1207":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Re-run install for missing managed directories or required files; use `--reinstall` for other damage","locale":"en"},"1208":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Interrupted install left .stage / .old","locale":"en"},"1209":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Repeat the same install; it cleans staging and restores the old tree when needed","locale":"en"},"1210":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"External directory moved","locale":"en"},"1211":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Update the reference with `import --dir NEW --name NAME`","locale":"en"},"1212":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"A reference file is broken","locale":"en"},"1213":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Fix it or delete it with `remove NAME`; other directories remain usable","locale":"en"},"1214":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"External toolchain missing from list","locale":"en"},"1215":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Reference the existing directory with `import --dir PATH --name NAME`","locale":"en"},"1216":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Update asset/digest missing","locale":"en"},"1217":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Check that the release includes an EXE matching the program architecture and a SHA-256 digest","locale":"en"},"1218":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Windows self removal failed","locale":"en"},"1219":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Read failure.txt in the reported directory, close occupying processes and rerun uninstall.ps1","locale":"en"},"1220":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Keep the complete error, command, shell identity and `hanamori --version`. `config show --resolved` shows configuration sources. `doctor --json` diagnoses without repairs and still returns nonzero on errors. Logs may include complete request URLs.","locale":"en"},"1221":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Imports cannot be deleted with `uninstall`; use `remove` to unregister them. An existing lock file does not imply a held lock. Do not remove locks to bypass contention. Doctor checks layout and required files, without hashing every installed file. Earlier completed removals are not rolled back when a later step fails.","locale":"en"},"1222":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","type":"page","content":"Self-update","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Maintenance and reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/upgrade","locale":"en"},"1223":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-0","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"Update a Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC build from a verified GitHub Release.","locale":"en"},"1224":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-1","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC builds can update the executable that is currently running from the\nlatest stable GitHub Release:","locale":"en"},"1225":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-2","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"`--check` reports the current version, latest version and executable path without\ndownloading an executable or writing files. An equal version normally needs no update;\n`--force` allows reinstalling it. Neither mode downgrades a newer build, selects a\nprerelease, or bypasses verification. `--check` and `--force` cannot be combined.","locale":"en"},"1226":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-3","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"The updater downloads the EXE matching the running executable architecture directly. The Release asset\nmust supply a SHA-256 digest; its hash and size must match, and the candidate must\nsuccessfully report the expected `hanamori --version` within ten seconds. Missing or\ninvalid metadata, download errors and failed verification leave the current executable\nin place. The next invocation after a successful update uses the new version.","locale":"en"},"1227":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-4","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"The existing `--proxy`, `HANAMORI_PROXY` and configuration `proxy` setting apply to both\nthe API query and download. Optional `GITHUB_TOKEN` authenticates only the API request;\nit is not sent to the asset download. Toolchain mirrors, caches, download directories\nand project files do not control self-update. Other platforms/build targets currently\nhave no self-update asset.","locale":"en"},"1228":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-5","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"Updating requires write access to the executable's directory. Staging is created beside\nthat executable, and a sibling `<executable>.update.lock` prevents simultaneous updates.\nThe lock file may remain after completion; do not delete it to bypass an active update.\nThe old executable is renamed to `<executable>.outdated`, retained while its process\nexits, and removed by the next actual update. After verifying the new executable, if backup\ndeletion is blocked by file usage, Windows Restart Manager closes its users and retries.\nResolve any remaining error manually. These sibling names are reserved for the updater.","locale":"en"},"1229":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-6","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"Replacement failure attempts to restore the original executable. The two renames are\nnot one atomic operation: if the process is terminated between them and the original\npath is missing, rename `<executable>.outdated` back to the original name before retrying.\nA reported rollback failure also gives the exact restore paths. Self-update does not\nchange registered toolchains or shell configuration.","locale":"en"},"1230":{"id":"/en/docs/upgrade-7","page_id":"/en/docs/upgrade","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/upgrade","content":"Self-update preserves the running executable architecture: x64 builds select the x64 asset; ARM64 builds select `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe`, without switching according to OS architecture.","locale":"en"},"1231":{"id":"/en/docs/website","page_id":"/en/docs/website","type":"page","content":"Website maintenance","breadcrumbs":["Hanamori Documentation","Development"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/website","locale":"en"},"1232":{"id":"/en/docs/website-0","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website","content":"Maintain the home page, downloads, bilingual docs and static deployments.","locale":"en"},"1233":{"id":"/en/docs/website-1","page_id":"/en/docs/website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"Content and configuration","locale":"en"},"1234":{"id":"/en/docs/website-2","page_id":"/en/docs/website","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/website#build-and-deployment","content":"Build and deployment","locale":"en"},"1235":{"id":"/en/docs/website-3","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website","content":"The independent `site/` project adapts RVC Next’s Fumadocs/TanStack Start framework. It uses React, Tailwind, MDX, Bun and Vitest. Provenance and licensing are in `site/NOTICE` and `site/LICENSE`.","locale":"en"},"1236":{"id":"/en/docs/website-4","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website","content":"Development runs at `127.0.0.1:3000`; static output is `.output/public`. On a fresh checkout, generate routes by building or starting dev before a type check if needed. Do not edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts` manually or commit caches/build output.","locale":"en"},"1237":{"id":"/en/docs/website-5","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"`content/docs/PAGE.mdx` is Chinese and `PAGE.en.mdx` is English, each with title/description frontmatter.","locale":"en"},"1238":{"id":"/en/docs/website-6","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"`meta.json` and `meta.en.json` use the same slug order. Links use `/docs/PAGE`; language switches in place, without separate language routes.","locale":"en"},"1239":{"id":"/en/docs/website-7","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"Home copy is in `src/lib/site-copy.ts`; components live under `src/components/`.","locale":"en"},"1240":{"id":"/en/docs/website-8","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"`src/lib/releases.ts` accepts exact named assets from stable releases, distinguishing query errors from unavailable downloads.","locale":"en"},"1241":{"id":"/en/docs/website-9","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"Escape literal angle brackets/braces in MDX prose, or put them inside code blocks.","locale":"en"},"1242":{"id":"/en/docs/website-10","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#content-and-configuration","content":"The Umami analytics script and website ID are configured in `src/routes/__root.tsx`. Documentation comments use the `Comment` category in Hanamori’s GitHub Discussions, configured in `src/lib/giscus.ts`. Giscus maps discussions by pathname, uses Chinese (`zh-CN`), and follows the system color scheme. No comment-related environment variables are required.","locale":"en"},"1243":{"id":"/en/docs/website-11","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#build-and-deployment","content":"The pinned static Server Function middleware requests its cache from the root path. A build transform in `vite.config.ts` prefixes client requests with the base path while keeping cache files at the output root. Recheck documentation navigation under a subpath when upgrading this dependency.","locale":"en"},"1244":{"id":"/en/docs/website-12","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#build-and-deployment","content":"Custom-domain/root deployments use the default `/`. Static preparation verifies home, download, docs and search output and creates the 404 fallback. New top-level routes must be added to prerender configuration and output checks.","locale":"en"},"1245":{"id":"/en/docs/website-13","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#build-and-deployment","content":"The site workflow validates builds for pull requests. Website changes on main or a manual run on main also force-push `.output/public` to the `gh-pages` branch after validation, using the repository secret `GITEE_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY`. The key needs repository write access. In the repository Pages settings, select `Deploy from a branch`, the `gh-pages` branch, and `/ (root)`. Netlify, Cloudflare Pages and Vercel configuration uses the same `.output/public` output and requires separate platform setup.","locale":"en"},"1246":{"id":"/en/docs/website-14","page_id":"/en/docs/website","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/website#build-and-deployment","content":"Check both `/` and `/Hanamori/`: deep-link refreshes, languages, search navigation, theme, mobile layout, reduced motion, and download states for unavailable releases, network errors and matching assets. A working development server is not evidence of a working static deployment.","locale":"en"}},"count":1246},"sorting":{"language":"multilingual","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":936,"2":885,"3":1038,"4":111,"5":978,"6":934,"7":1108,"8":714,"9":1185,"10":259,"11":918,"12":1033,"13":1120,"14":1174,"15":967,"16":498,"17":163,"18":1191,"19":0,"20":340,"21":114,"22":831,"23":1,"24":376,"25":126,"26":1128,"27":499,"28":452,"29":154,"30":1173,"31":500,"32":754,"33":262,"34":1145,"35":501,"36":736,"37":254,"38":902,"39":509,"40":466,"41":156,"42":1087,"43":508,"44":336,"45":129,"46":992,"47":1051,"48":1097,"49":900,"50":1227,"51":1132,"52":281,"