n global configuration or missing installation."],[1047,"Actual four-part version; `null` means no SDK; omitted means unconstrained"],[769,"Actual SDK version; conflicts with sdk-id and no-sdk"],[979,"Actual version"],[1116,"Add `--completions` to `hanamori env` to register Tab completion with the hook. This is opt-in and supports PowerShell, Bash and Zsh; Zsh requires `compinit` first. Standalone `hanamori completions` is also available. See terminal completion."],[1096,"After checks pass, the selected channels build and publish from the same commit. Ordinary branch CI does not respond to tag pushes; the two channels in one Release run share checks instead of running `cargo test` separately."],[699,"After replacing an old hook, call the new executable directly to regenerate and load `env`, or rerun `shell init` to update persistent entries. For example, invoke `/d/Tools/hanamori.exe` in Git Bash/Zsh, quoting paths containing spaces. INCLUDE/LIB consumed by the compiler retain Windows syntax; do not convert every variable to POSIX paths."],[955,"After updating Hanamori, a session-variable mismatch requires opening a fresh terminal from the desktop or Start menu and running `hanamori use` again. A child shell launched from the current terminal inherits the old state. This error does not indicate damaged toolchains: MSVC, SDK and MSBuild do not need reinstalling. Hanamori does not guess missing original environment values from older sessions."],[633,"Aliases and defaults"],[679,"all layers"],[946,"All local commands and dynamic completion use the configured `toolchains_dir`. Files in `references` name targets; deleting a reference does not delete a toolchain, and deleting a toolchain does not leave a database entry that can block reinstall."],[748,"All public commands, defaults, conflicts and output conventions."],[870,"All three shells support these local candidates. The next Tab press reads changes after an installation, import or alias update without regenerating the script."],[1019,"Also clean managed tools, complete cache entries, config and references; preserve external tools"],[1198,"Ambiguous version prefix"],[956,"An MSBuild-enabled selection additionally manages `VSINSTALLDIR`, `VCTargetsPath`, `MSBuildExtensionsPath`, `MSBuildExtensionsPath32`, `ForceImportAfterCppDefaultProps`, `ForceImportAfterCppTargets`, `UseEnv`, `DisableRegistryUse` and `PreferredToolArchitecture`, and adds its private `MSBuild/Current/Bin/amd64` to PATH. Switching to an ordinary combination clears these settings; deactivation restores their original values. The `msbuild` field in `list/current --json` records the selected version."],[1089,"An optional existing `v*` Git tag, such as `v0.1.0`. If omitted, the highest `v*` tag in Git version order is selected, independently of tag creation dates or GitHub Release dates."],[44,"application"],[676,"application"],[639,"Architecture"],[1153,"Architecture acceptance"],[20,"archive"],[652,"archive"],[1133,"Area"],[904,"Arguments after `exec --`"],[532,"ARM64 Host 工具需要 Windows 11 ARM64。微软从 VS 2022 17.4 开始提供原生 ARM64 Visual Studio 工具，详见 Visual Studio on Arm devices。Hanamori 分别选择 Host 编译器与 Target 库。"],[708,"ARM64 program builds"],[739,"ARM64 releases provide `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` and `.zip`; the ZIP contains `hanamori.exe`. Source builds use `cargo build --release --target aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` with the corresponding MSVC linker."],[107,"ARM64 发布包含 `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` 和 `.zip`，ZIP 内为 `hanamori.exe`。源码构建使用 `cargo build --release --target aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`，并准备相应的 MSVC 链接器。"],[77,"ARM64 程序版本"],[1149,"ARM64-hosted tools require Windows 11 ARM64. Microsoft introduced native ARM64 Visual Studio tools in VS 2022 17.4; see Visual Studio on Arm devices. Hanamori selects the host compiler and target libraries independently."],[1114,"Automatic project switching"],[730,"Bash also supports `HANAMORI_INSTALL_DIR`, with `--install-dir` taking precedence. An unset or empty variable uses the default directory. For a piped installation, pass the variable to `bash`:"],[693,"Bash and Zsh"],[1125,"Bash and Zsh:"],[62,"Bash 与 Zsh"],[99,"Bash 同样支持 `HANAMORI_INSTALL_DIR`，`--install-dir` 优先于环境变量。变量未设置或为空时使用默认目录；管道安装时将变量传给 `bash`："],[865,"Bash:"],[237,"Bash："],[895,"Bash/Zsh offer declared choices for options such as `--vs-version`, `--channel` and `--shell`"],[897,"Bash/Zsh use path hints and shell filename completion; the shell handles spaces"],[502,"Bash/Zsh 中使用 `hanamori env --output hanamori-init.sh && . ./hanamori-init.sh`。"],[269,"Bash/Zsh 使用路径提示与 Shell 的文件补全；包含空格的路径由 Shell 处理"],[267,"Bash/Zsh 提供 `--vs-version`、`--channel`、`--shell` 等命令定义中的候选"],[1023,"Before replacing a directory on Windows, Hanamori registers the old installation's files with Windows Restart Manager, queries their users, logs process names and PIDs, and requests shutdown. Unresponsive processes are forcibly closed. Selection is scoped to the installation's files, rather than globally terminating processes named `MSBuild.exe`, `mspdbsrv.exe` or `vctip.exe`. The PDB server and telemetry program from the Microsoft packages remain installed."],[891,"Behavior"],[1009,"Behavior"],[869,"Both `hanamori` and `hanamori.exe` are registered, including the function installed by the hook. An executable outside PATH can still generate scripts when invoked by its path. Use a POSIX path understood by your shell in Windows Bash/Zsh."],[786,"Both commands accept `--vs-version 2022/2026` (aliases 17/18; default 2026), `--channel release/preview` (aliases stable/insiders; default release), `--manifest URL` (conflicts with both) and `--strict-manifest-integrity`. Install has no `--json` option."],[796,"Both positionals together assign; otherwise lists mappings"],[1234,"Build and deployment"],[706,"Build from source"],[689,"CAB files are read in offset order within each compressed folder, keeping one decoder\nalive across files instead of restarting it for every file. The backend is pinned to\n`cab-superewald 0.6.1`, which exposes folder readers and retains Stored, MSZIP and LZX\ndecoding. Only one cabinet is open at a time, and file contents are streamed rather than\nbuffered in full."],[58,"CAB 按压缩文件夹中的偏移顺序连续读取，多个文件复用同一解压器，避免每提取一个文件都从头解压。后端固定为提供文件夹读取接口的 `cab-superewald 0.6.1`，保留原有 Stored、MSZIP 和 LZX 解码支持。每次只打开一个 CAB，文件内容不再整体缓存在内存中。"],[889,"Candidate lookup resolves `toolchains_dir` from CLI, environment, configuration and defaults. It does not parse unrelated proxy/log settings or project files, download manifests, write files or acquire locks. One malformed reference is skipped without hiding other installations. Unreadable storage suppresses relevant local candidates while static completion remains available. Manually saved scripts invoke the executable path used at generation time; regenerate them if you move the program."],[872,"Candidates"],[1200,"Cannot map actual version to download ID"],[24,"catalog"],[656,"catalog"],[658,"Catalog parsing and package selection"],[802,"Change this shell through a loaded hook; accepts direct-directory options below"],[1185,"Check --manager-dir / HANAMORI_HOME / platform defaults and check toolchains_dir and inspect directories/references with list or doctor; shared, ambiguous versions are not suggested"],[1246,"Check both `/` and `/Hanamori/`: deep-link refreshes, languages, search navigation, theme, mobile layout, reduced motion, and download states for unavailable releases, network errors and matching assets. A working development server is not evidence of a working static deployment."],[1217,"Check that the release includes an EXE matching the program architecture and a SHA-256 digest"],[1078,"Checks, builds and publication"],[1197,"Choose `--shell-executable pwsh` or `powershell.exe`, or use `--profile`"],[1177,"Choose diagnostics and recovery steps based on the actual failure."],[1082,"Choose one bump command. It updates `workspace.package.version` in `Cargo.toml` and uses\nCargo to regenerate the workspace entries in `Cargo.lock`, preserving locked dependency\nversions. It does not commit changes or create tags. Commit the version change before tagging:"],[1118,"Choose the command for your shell and reopen it. Temporary hooks also accept `env --use-on-cd`.\nThis includes initial selection at startup, so `--auto-activate` is unnecessary. It conflicts\nwith `--dir`, which binds a fixed toolchain directory."],[1027,"Choose the right 5.1/7 profile and pass scripts and arguments correctly."],[1173,"CI runs on Linux, native Windows x64 and `windows-11-arm`. Archive tests cover all four host/target pairs for VS 2022 and VS 2026, including MSBuild, independent directory identities and required-file checks."],[1157,"CI uses the existing Linux and Windows workflow. Tests use real implementation paths,\nlocal HTTP servers, synthetic archives and real available shells. Required-shell mode\nprevents silently treating missing shells as successful integration coverage."],[560,"CI 包含 Linux、原生 Windows x64 和 `windows-11-arm`。解包测试覆盖 VS 2022/2026 的四种 Host/Target 组合、MSBuild、独立目录身份及必要文件检查。"],[1015,"Clean complete download cache entries without changing installations"],[745,"Cleanup recognizes complete files only in the fixed SHA-256 namespace. It preserves unknown files, partial downloads, directories and locks. Entries locked by another Hanamori operation are skipped. On Windows, after acquiring the cache lock, a deletion blocked by file usage closes that file's users through Windows Restart Manager and retries. Incomplete cleanup returns a nonzero status and reports completed removals. Resolve contention and retry. It does not modify toolchains or references or persistent workspaces. Previews take no locks, write no files and close no processes."],[289,"CLI / JSON 字段"],[944,"CLI relative paths resolve against the invocation directory; file paths resolve against\nthe manager directory; environment paths must be absolute. Tildes and variable expressions\nare not expanded by Hanamori. Configuration queries, help and version do not create storage.\nLocal selection does not parse unused proxy/download settings. Settings contain preferences,\nnot aliases, project declarations or session state."],[316,"CLI 相对路径基于当前工作目录，配置文件中的路径基于管理器目录，环境路径必须为绝对路径。Hanamori 不展开 `~` 或变量表达式。`--proxy` 为 HTTP(S) 代理；mirror 只影响工具链负载 URL，不控制自我更新。"],[917,"CLI/config field"],[278,"CMD / Fish"],[906,"CMD / Fish"],[847,"CMD integration"],[849,"CMD uses a batch entry and DOSKEY macro, not POSIX evaluation. Inside another batch file,\nuse `call \"%_HANAMORI_CMD_ENTRY%\" use stable` rather than relying on interactive DOSKEY.\nTo maintain the current user's AutoRun entry on native Windows:"],[223,"CMD 仍为实验性支持。代码页、引号、交互 DOSKEY、批处理和 AutoRun 的 Windows 原生验收与交叉编译是不同事项。"],[217,"CMD 使用批处理和 DOSKEY 宏，不能使用 POSIX 的 eval。先生成并调用入口："],[215,"CMD 集成"],[1145,"Combinations"],[789,"Command"],[809,"Command"],[826,"Command"],[1008,"Command"],[678,"Command line, configuration, self-update and self-uninstall"],[747,"Command reference"],[758,"Command/option"],[892,"Commands and options"],[742,"Complete payloads are stored by SHA-256 content identity after verification. Corrupt entries are fetched again. Independent installations can reuse these files without sharing installed SDK directories."],[998,"Component selection follows explicit command-line options, then project settings, then defaults. Projects may set `\"msbuild\": true` or `false`; `--msbuild` / `--no-msbuild` override that setting. An explicit MSBuild requirement without the SDK fails; use `--no-msbuild` to cancel that requirement. Exact directory keys retain their component combination, so the new default does not add MSBuild to an existing key."],[912,"Configuration and storage"],[839,"Configuration table by default; `--resolved` includes sources and derived paths; `--json` prints JSON"],[1101,"Configure `CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN` in the repository's Actions Secrets with a crates.io API token authorized to publish `hanamori`. The first publication requires permission to create the crate; subsequent publications require permission to publish that crate."],[890,"Content"],[1233,"Content and configuration"],[1079,"crates.io credentials and retries"],[459,"crates.io 凭据与重试"],[478,"crates.io 渠道运行 `cargo publish --locked`，保留包内源码的编译验证，仅发布 `hanamori`，不发布 `hanamori-test-support` 或 `xtask`。"],[1069,"Create `hello.cpp`:"],[794,"Current fixed session snapshot, without reselecting project/default"],[1134,"Current scope"],[1244,"Custom-domain/root deployments use the default `/`. Static preparation verifies home, download, docs and search output and creates the 404 fallback. New top-level routes must be added to prerender configuration and output checks."],[1109,"Deactivate the current session first and close other terminals using Hanamori. Toolchain\nor cache cleanup failures stop before deleting the program and remaining manager metadata.\nEarlier completed removals are not rolled back. `--purge` reuses the file usage handling from toolchain uninstall and cache cleanup. Resolve the reported error before retrying. Incomplete managed directories can still be uninstalled. A dry run performs no writes, registry edits, lock acquisition, process shutdown or helper launch."],[919,"Default"],[700,"Default Bash setup maintains `.bashrc` and a login-profile bridge without repeating user settings in login/non-login sessions. With no usable login file, it creates the lowest-priority `.profile`. Deinitialization can delete that generated file if it becomes empty, retaining user additions. Zsh respects `ZDOTDIR`; explicit `--profile` takes precedence."],[785,"Defaults to VS 2026; `--all` queries VS 2022 and 2026; optional `--toolset-id ID` inspects a selected toolset; supports `--json`"],[1013,"Delete a managed directory and references to it; reject external targets"],[1011,"Delete one reference; preserve files and other references"],[1206,"Deleted files prevent use"],[638,"Deleting a directory leaves references dangling without blocking reinstallation. Reinstalling the same key restores them. One malformed reference does not hide other installations; doctor reports it."],[1236,"Development runs at `127.0.0.1:3000`; static output is `.output/public`. On a fresh checkout, generate routes by building or starting dev before a type check if needed. Do not edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts` manually or commit caches/build output."],[987,"Different architecture pairs have separate directories and can coexist. For external directories with several pairs,\nuse `--dir PATH --arch HOST/TARGET` with `env`, `use`, `exec`, `import` or `doctor`.\nUnavailable catalog pairs fail explicitly; Hanamori does not substitute another architecture."],[808,"Direct-directory options are `--dir/-d PATH`, `--toolset VER`, `--sdk VER`, `--no-sdk` and `--arch HOST/TARGET`. These selectors require dir, and sdk conflicts with no-sdk. Explicit SELECTOR or exec’s using conflicts with all directory options. Component selectors use actual directory versions."],[820,"Direct-directory options, `--shell/-s`, `--output/-o` or `--plain`"],[719,"Directory containing `hanamori.exe`"],[666,"Directory discovery, named references, projects and local selection"],[982,"Directory key"],[900,"Directory keys, aliases and installed versions"],[885,"Directory version completion applies to `use`, `exec`, `import`, `env`, `shell activate` and `shell init`, including unregistered directories. These are actual installed versions such as `14.44.35207` and `10.0.26100.0`, not remote download IDs. The second argument of `alias` creates a new name and does not suggest selectors. Installation and remote catalog commands do not mix in local versions either."],[981,"Directory version verified after extraction"],[777,"Disable MSBuild, overriding the default and the project; keeps the compiler and SDK by default"],[792,"Discovered directories, aliases, actual versions and availability; no network"],[1031,"Discovery queries that runtime’s user profile with profiles disabled. A discovery failure does not silently edit another runtime’s profile; use `--profile PATH` for an explicit file. Existing UTF-16 encoding is preserved."],[1132,"Distinguish program builds, shell integration and native MSVC execution."],[1137,"Distribution and self-update"],[1029,"Dot-sourcing lets the script modify this shell. Do not source an old output file after generation fails. Execution policy may restrict script loading; follow your system’s policy. Hanamori does not permanently relax it for you."],[28,"download"],[660,"download"],[1204,"Download failure"],[976,"Download ID"],[691,"Download integrity, archive checksums and output path checks remain enabled. Before publication, the engine checks actual versions and required compiler, header and library files. It does not generate a full file inventory or hash the installed tree."],[740,"Downloads, cache and proxy"],[1022,"Downloads, extraction and required-file checks finish before replacing an old managed tree. The new tree is staged on the destination volume. Publication renames the old tree aside and moves the new one into place, restoring the old tree on failure. The next installation for that target handles interrupted `.stage` / `.old` directories. Doctor reports issues without changing files."],[1156,"Dynamic parsing uses a pinned `clap_complete` Rust engine; its `unstable-dynamic` feature\nis not exposed as a public shell protocol. The internal `shell complete` command only\nqueries candidates. Shell adapter templates live in `src/commands/completions/`, while\nstatic command completion still comes from the same Clap tree. Check both template\nadaptation and dynamic parsing when upgrading; do not edit generated scripts manually."],[1126,"Each command selects its manager through `--manager-dir`, then `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform default (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori` on Windows). A generation-time `--manager-dir` does not pin future commands. Set `HANAMORI_HOME` in your startup configuration to persist a custom manager directory. An explicit `env --dir PATH` supplies a toolchain directory default for calls without an explicit selector; it does not register that directory."],[685,"Each managed combination occupies `<toolchains-dir>/<source>/msvc-<download ID>_sdk-<ID or none>_host-<host>_target-<target>`. Local commands discover directories and check a small set of required files. Directory names retain download IDs; actual compiler and SDK versions come from the extracted tree. Custom source identity is a stable SHA-256 of the manifest URL, independent of changing manifest contents."],[968,"Each owned installation has an exclusive directory. Imports are read-only references. Selecting tools never downloads them, and installing tools does not activate the current terminal. Native compilation supports Windows x64 / ARM64 hosts and x64 / ARM64 targets; tests on other platforms do not establish MSVC execution support. See platform support."],[853,"Enable command, option and path completion in PowerShell, Bash and Zsh."],[855,"Enable in this session only"],[854,"Enable with shell initialization"],[40,"engine"],[672,"engine"],[918,"Environment"],[947,"Environment and session reference"],[1241,"Escape literal angle brackets/braces in MDX prose, or put them inside code blocks."],[767,"Exact download ID; conflicts with positional VERSION"],[763,"Exact final directory instead of independent managed storage"],[974,"Example"],[985,"Examples describe version syntax; availability depends on the selected catalog."],[773,"Exclude the SDK and, by default, MSBuild; add `--no-msbuild` if the project explicitly requires MSBuild"],[878,"Existing named references"],[848,"Experimental batch entry, DOSKEY and current-user AutoRun."],[775,"Explicitly enable MSBuild, overriding the project; enabled with the SDK by default, for VS 2022 v143 and VS 2026 v145; conflicts with `--no-sdk` and `--no-msbuild`"],[1210,"External directory moved"],[1214,"External toolchain missing from list"],[641,"Extraction and publication"],[1042,"Field"],[896,"Files and directories"],[1002,"FileTracker uses the private directory instead of a system installation. Its upstream implementation has an ANSI-path restriction, so this initial version recommends an ASCII toolchain installation path such as `--dir D:/Tools/hanamori-build`. Unicode project directories are a separate case."],[378,"FileTracker 使用私有目录，不借用系统安装。其上游实现有 ANSI 路径限制，首版建议将 MSBuild 工具链安装在 ASCII 路径下，例如 `--dir D:/Tools/hanamori-build`；这与项目目录含 Unicode 是两个不同的情况。"],[1060,"First compilation"],[873,"First positional argument of `use`, `default`, `alias`"],[1213,"Fix it or delete it with `remove NAME`; other directories remain usable"],[1203,"Fix it; it is not skipped in favor of a parent/default"],[765,"Fixed alias; does not activate or change default"],[894,"Fixed values"],[1167,"For actual compiler acceptance, install or import two real MSVC/SDK combinations on native\nWindows. Both compiler and SDK directory versions must differ. Use managed directory keys from `list` or named references:"],[736,"For future sessions, add that directory to your user PATH through Windows Environment Variables. Shell initialization creates a command hook; it does not install the executable or permanently edit PATH."],[1158,"For main pushes and pull requests, Rust CI runs only when Rust source, Rust tests, workspace\npackages, Cargo/toolchain configuration or related release automation change. The Installers\nworkflow checks the root installer scripts and `tests/installers/`; Rust source and build\nconfiguration changes also trigger installer integration checks. Website checks `site/` and\nrebuilds distributed installer files when the scripts change. README-only, website-only and\ninstaller-only changes skip Rust CI. Release calls Rust CI and Installers with the same source\ncommit and requires both to pass before publishing, regardless of changed-path filters."],[1159,"For ordinary local checks, run `cargo test --workspace`. Unavailable optional shells are\nreported as skipped; an explicitly configured runtime must exist. Windows Bash/Zsh tests\nneed Git Bash or MSYS2 with `cygpath`, rather than WSL. Test subprocesses retain a usable\nWindows temporary directory while isolating Hanamori state and configuration. CMD lifecycle\nfixtures use a small system PATH so the developer's installed tools do not consume the\nbatch command length limit."],[1030,"For persistent setup, choose the runtime you actually use:"],[735,"For the current PowerShell session:"],[16,"foundation"],[27,"foundation"],[31,"foundation"],[35,"foundation"],[648,"foundation"],[659,"foundation"],[663,"foundation"],[667,"foundation"],[675,"foundation, archive, catalog, download, state"],[671,"foundation, state"],[43,"foundation、archive、catalog、download、state"],[39,"foundation、state"],[856,"Generate a standalone script"],[967,"Get Hanamori from the download page, or build from source."],[1067,"Get Hanamori, add its executable directory to PATH, and open PowerShell in a writable project directory. These commands use the default VS 2026 stable catalog. Installation needs network access and disk space."],[631,"GitHub Actions 的 site workflow 在 PR 中验证构建；main 分支的网站变更或在 main 上手动运行工作流时，验证通过后使用仓库密钥 `GITEE_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY` 将 `.output/public` 强制推送到 `gh-pages` 分支。密钥需要具有仓库写入权限，仓库 Pages 的 Source 选择 `Deploy from a branch`，分支选择 `gh-pages`，目录选择 `/ (root)`。Netlify、Cloudflare Pages 和 Vercel 的配置同样使用 `.output/public`，需要各平台分别配置项目。"],[477,"GitHub 渠道分别在 Windows x64 和 `windows-11-arm` 构建 `hanamori-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe`、`hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` 及各自同名 ZIP。ZIP 内为 `hanamori.exe`；四个资产都验证 GitHub 报告的 SHA-256 digest。"],[749,"Global options"],[913,"Global options, environment variables, precedence and directory layout."],[964,"Hanamori documentation"],[860,"Hanamori generates completion scripts from the current build's command definitions. Tab completes public commands, nested subcommands and options. Generation needs no installed toolchain, network access or manager configuration."],[966,"Hanamori installs MSVC and the Windows SDK in independent directories without a Visual Studio installation. Select a toolchain by alias or project file, activate the current terminal, or prepare an environment for one build command."],[949,"Hanamori prepares PATH, INCLUDE, LIB, `CC`, `CXX`, `VCToolsVersion`, `VCToolsInstallDir`, `VCINSTALLDIR`, `VSCMD_ARG_HOST_ARCH`, `VSCMD_ARG_TGT_ARCH`, `DISTUTILS_USE_SDK`, and SDK root/bin/version variables when an SDK is selected."],[232,"Hanamori 从当前版本的命令定义生成补全脚本。按 Tab 可以补全公开命令、嵌套子命令和选项；生成脚本无需安装工具链、读取管理器配置或访问网络。按 Tab 查询本地候选时，只读取相关存储路径配置。"],[322,"Hanamori 准备 PATH、INCLUDE、LIB、`CC`、`CXX`、`VCToolsVersion`、`VCToolsInstallDir`、`VCINSTALLDIR`、`VSCMD_ARG_HOST_ARCH`、`VSCMD_ARG_TGT_ARCH`、`DISTUTILS_USE_SDK`，以及安装了 SDK 时所需的 SDK 根目录、bin 和版本变量。"],[339,"Hanamori 在独立目录中安装 MSVC 与 Windows SDK，不需要安装 Visual Studio。你可以通过别名或项目文件选择工具链，切换当前终端环境，或为一个构建命令临时准备环境。"],[337,"Hanamori 文档"],[1239,"Home copy is in `src/lib/site-copy.ts`; components live under `src/components/`."],[824,"Hook directory defaults use `--dir PATH` (no short `-d` here), `--toolset VER`, `--sdk VER` or `--no-sdk`. Component options require dir; sdk and no-sdk conflict. Each command selects the manager through `--manager-dir`, `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform default. Hook, completion and startup generation do not save a manager directory. Output defaults to stdout; when writing CMD output to a file, its path must end in `.cmd/.bat`. Hidden dispatch/run subcommands serve hooks, not the public interface."],[973,"Identifier"],[978,"Identifier offered by the selected catalog"],[910,"If no candidates appear, verify that you loaded the script for the correct shell and that your binary provides `completions`. In Zsh, initialize completion and reload the script if you see the `compinit` hint. For missing local candidates, check manager selection and diagnose directories and references with `list --json` / `doctor --json`; completion itself keeps these errors quiet. After an upgrade, regenerate manual scripts or open a new terminal using the startup loader."],[954,"If session state is invalid, avoid stacking activations. Retain the error and inspect installation/startup settings from a clean terminal. Removing startup entries does not restore the current environment, so deactivate before uninstalling."],[844,"Import has no dry-run option; importing the same name updates that reference. Catalog queries and installation may access the network; local management does not automatically install. Do not assume every command supports json or dry-run."],[1007,"Import requires `--name`. It checks the selected combination and saves only its path and actual versions under the manager's `references/`. External files are untouched. Importing again updates that name: after moving an external directory, import its new path with the same name. Different combinations may have separate names."],[1003,"Import, reinstall and remove"],[1221,"Imports cannot be deleted with `uninstall`; use `remove` to unregister them. An existing lock file does not imply a held lock. Do not remove locks to bypass contention. Doctor checks layout and required files, without hashing every installed file. Earlier completed removals are not rolled back when a later step fails."],[1085,"In Actions, choose **Release → Run workflow** and use the workflow on `main`:"],[863,"In Zsh, place the Hanamori startup block after `compinit` or your framework's completion initialization. If initialization is missing, Hanamori prints a hint and skips completion while keeping the toolchain hook usable. It does not run `compinit` for you."],[1146,"Independent MSVC/SDK directories; compiler-only supported; no sharing of installed SDK files"],[845,"Information commands use aligned tables or labeled fields by default. `list` marks active and default entries, while `alias` and `default` show target status; directory paths appear on their own lines. Use the command's `--json` option for programmatic access. Disabling logging does not hide query results."],[953,"Initial activation saves the environment baseline. Switching preserves that baseline, and deactivation restores original values rather than guessing PATH. `exec` uses the same preparation logic but applies it only to the child. Internal `_HANAMORI_*` state is for hooks and child processes, not user configuration; do not construct or edit it manually."],[1117,"Initialize once in each shell. By default, initialization only loads the hook; it does not\nselect an installation, inspect a project, or access the network. `--auto-activate` calls\n`use` once when loading into an inactive session; failure leaves the terminal usable.\nOpt into `--use-on-cd` to follow project toolchains as the working directory changes."],[1113,"Initialize, activate and restore a terminal environment."],[1086,"Input"],[871,"Input position"],[1199,"Inspect `list --json` and use an exact managed directory key or fixed alias"],[1205,"Inspect the reported URL, proxy and network; distinguish cache from workspace"],[1061,"Install a toolchain, compile a complete C++ example and run it."],[1034,"Install and remove dynamic startup loaders."],[1174,"Install each pair on a compatible compiler host, set `HANAMORI_TEST_MANAGER_DIR` and `HANAMORI_TEST_TOOLCHAIN_A` to that installation, then run:"],[702,"Install Hanamori or build from source"],[969,"Install toolchains and select versions"],[725,"Install toolchains when needed with `hanamori install latest --name stable`. Use `hanamori upgrade` for later updates and `hanamori self uninstall` for removal. Self uninstall removes installer-owned PATH entries using the adjacent `.install.json` receipt."],[703,"Install with PowerShell, download a portable executable, or build with Rust."],[965,"Install, select and manage standalone MSVC and Windows SDK combinations."],[750,"Installation and remote catalogs"],[757,"Installation includes MSVC + Windows SDK + MSBuild by default. Install help groups destination, versions and components, installation behavior, and catalog options."],[997,"Installation includes MSVC, the Windows SDK and MSBuild by default, selecting MSBuild 18.x (VS 2026) or 17.x (VS 2022), C++ props/targets, task assemblies and FileTracker from the same catalog. `--no-msbuild` excludes MSBuild and keeps the compiler and SDK. `--no-sdk` or project `\"sdk\": null` defaults to a compiler-only installation."],[1160,"Installer tests run through `tests/installers/run.mjs`, using only Node built-in modules,\nwithout website dependencies. The portable suite needs Node, Bash and PowerShell 7, but\ndoes not need Cargo or a Hanamori executable. It checks arguments, platform rejection,\nrelease metadata, architecture selection and preservation after a corrupt download:"],[996,"Installing an exact directory key fixes its source and download IDs. A custom-source key also requires its original `--manifest URL`. A project’s version constraints apply to version-based requests; an explicit key selects its own combination."],[1208,"Interrupted install left .stage / .old"],[1189,"Invoke the EXE directly; inspect PATH; reopen the terminal after persistent changes"],[1195,"Invoke the new EXE directly, check `cygpath`, reload env / rerun shell init"],[957,"It also sets and manages `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1` so build nodes exit after a build instead of keeping the toolchain locked and preventing reinstallation. Parallel builds remain available, but subsequent builds cannot reuse earlier nodes. This applies to newly started builds and does not stop existing resident processes."],[951,"It does not generate `vcvarsall.bat` or `vcvars64.bat`. POSIX shells receive POSIX executable paths, while INCLUDE/LIB consumed by the compiler retain Windows paths."],[728,"It requires `cygpath`, `curl` and Windows PowerShell or PowerShell 7. If PowerShell is absent from the MSYS2 PATH, the script checks the Windows system directory. From a checkout, run `bash install.sh` to use the adjacent `install.ps1`."],[1220,"Keep the complete error, command, shell identity and `hanamori --version`. `config show --resolved` shows configuration sources. `doctor --json` diagnoses without repairs and still returns nonzero on errors. Logs may include complete request URLs."],[644,"Layer"],[753,"Lifecycle and cleanup"],[1143,"Linux/other Unix"],[526,"Linux/其他 Unix"],[694,"Load hooks, handle native Windows paths and configure login startup files."],[1181,"Load the completion script, or run `shell init --completions` and reopen the terminal; see terminal completion"],[1028,"Load the current terminal first:"],[751,"Local directories and selection"],[857,"Local dynamic candidates"],[1187,"Local dynamic candidates are supported; fixed enums and ordinary paths retain static-generator limitations"],[1148,"Local tests, cross-compilation and native Windows acceptance are different evidence. See testing and native acceptance for the verification procedure. A successful build does not establish acceptance for every shell or real compiler combination."],[846,"Logs use stderr; JSON and generated scripts use stdout. Exec’s child inherits streams. Failures return nonzero; do not source output from failed generation. Doctor still fails when its JSON reports errors. Previews can list blockers; execution requires resolving them. On Windows, scheduling self removal is not proof that the executable has already been deleted: the helper reports its own result."],[540,"main 推送和 PR 仅在 Rust 源码、Rust 测试、工作区包、Cargo/工具链配置或相关发布自动化发生变化时触发 Rust CI。根目录安装脚本和 `tests/installers/` 由 Installers 工作流单独检查；Rust 源码和构建配置变化也会触发安装集成验证。Website 工作流检查 `site/`，并在安装脚本变化时重新生成分发产物。只修改 README、网站或安装脚本不触发 Rust CI。Release 对 Rust CI 和 Installers 的复用调用使用同一提交，发布前必须全部通过，不受变更路径过滤影响。"],[1232,"Maintain the home page, downloads, bilingual docs and static deployments."],[1202,"Malformed nearest project file"],[1004,"Manage directory discovery, references and reinstallation."],[984,"Managed directory determined by source and download IDs"],[761,"Managed directory key, actual version/prefix or latest; project constraints apply; otherwise chooses the channel’s latest"],[874,"Managed directory keys, external reference keys, existing aliases (including default), unambiguous full MSVC directory versions"],[992,"Managed installations without MSBuild live under `<toolchains-dir>/<source>/msvc-<download-id>_sdk-<download-id-or-none>_host-x64_target-x64`. The default MSBuild combination also has a `_msbuild-<version>` segment. The default base is `<manager>/toolchains`. Custom sources use a stable digest of the manifest URL, not the changing catalog contents. Local commands and completion honor the configured storage directory too."],[887,"Manager selection consistently follows the already entered `--manager-dir`, then `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform default (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori` on Windows). Functions, direct executable calls and completion use the same rule. Changing HOME affects the next completion. A generation-time `--manager-dir` is not stored as a fallback manager."],[1121,"Manual `use` and `deactivate` remain effective until the next directory change. Reloading\ndoes not duplicate callbacks; loading a hook without `--use-on-cd` disables tracking while\nkeeping the active environment. Editing a project file without changing directories does\nnot refresh automatically; run `hanamori use`. See CMD integration for its limits."],[783,"May query manifests; no payload download, installation, reference or workspace writes"],[647,"May use"],[627,"MDX 正文中的尖括号、花括号需要转义或放入代码块，不能直接当普通 Markdown 使用。"],[715,"Meaning"],[759,"Meaning"],[975,"Meaning"],[1043,"Meaning"],[1087,"Meaning"],[1184,"Missing local versions or aliases"],[645,"Modules"],[971,"MSBuild and component selection"],[1025,"MSBuild combinations also check the engine, C++ targets, task assemblies, FileTracker and generated configuration. On Windows, doctor probes the engine version to distinguish runtime startup failures from missing files; other platforms only check files. Reinstall the full key from `list` to repair missing required components. Import preserves the MSBuild version of a Hanamori portable installation; it does not convert an arbitrary Visual Studio directory into a supported standalone MSBuild installation."],[686,"MSBuild combinations insert `_msbuild-<version>` before `_host-<host>_target-<target>`. `catalog/msbuild` selects explicit VS 2022/2026 C++ package sets without recursively installing arbitrary VS dependencies. Payload roles distinguish toolset, SDK and MSBuild; FileTracker's MSI is extracted separately and arranged beside the private engine. The foundation `msbuild` module generates local props/targets from source templates, records the engine package version and defines required-file checks. It does not modify upstream targets, write registry entries or invoke system installers."],[1000,"MSBuild combinations use `<source>/msvc-<ID>_sdk-<ID>_msbuild-<MSBuild version>_host-x64_target-x64`, independently of combinations without MSBuild. Reinstalling an exact key requires the catalog to still offer that MSBuild version; it never silently upgrades it. Retain a matching manifest and cache if upstream removes packages."],[347,"MSBuild 与组件选择"],[537,"MSBuild 原生验收"],[55,"MSBuild 组合在 `_host-<host>_target-<target>` 前加入 `_msbuild-<版本>`。`catalog/msbuild` 维护 VS 2022/2026 C++ 所需的明确包集合；不递归安装任意 VS 依赖。负载带 toolset/SDK/MSBuild 角色，FileTracker MSI 独立解包并整理到私有引擎目录。`msbuild` 模块从源模板生成安装内的 props/targets，保存引擎包版本并定义关键文件检查；不修改上游 targets，不写注册表，不运行系统安装器。"],[980,"MSVC `14.44.35207`, SDK `10.0.26100.0`"],[355,"MSVC `14.44.35207`，SDK `10.0.26100.0`"],[882,"MSVC directory versions in the specified directory"],[1142,"MSYS path conversion requires the current runtime’s `cygpath`"],[525,"MSYS 路径转换依赖当前运行时的 `cygpath`"],[705,"MSYS2 and Git Bash"],[74,"MSYS2 与 Git Bash"],[841,"Mutually exclusive `--check` or `--force`; Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC only"],[634,"Name fixed installations rather than chaining mutable aliases."],[637,"Names contain 1–64 letters, digits, hyphens or underscores, excluding command names. `default` is allowed. Removing a nonexistent name succeeds. `remove NAME` and `unalias NAME` remove only that reference. Uninstalling a managed directory removes its managed references."],[1135,"Native compilation"],[1152,"Native MSBuild acceptance"],[662,"Network transfers, integrity, ranges and cache"],[1179,"Next steps"],[682,"no dependency cycles between sibling modules at any depth, including code for other\nplatforms; test-only code is exempt;"],[905,"No Hanamori option suggestions; completion of the child program's arguments is outside this feature"],[903,"No network lookups; inspect `list-remote` instead"],[931,"None"],[934,"None"],[907,"Not currently provided; requesting CMD completion returns an explicit error"],[861,"Omitting `--shell` detects the calling shell; you can explicitly select `powershell`, `bash` or `zsh`. As with normal initialization, use `--profile PATH` or `--shell-executable PATH` to select the startup file/runtime, and `--dry-run` to preview changes."],[697,"Omitting `--shell` detects the calling shell. When explicitly generating a script, choose `--shell bash` or `--shell zsh` to match the shell that will source it."],[1119,"On directory changes, the nearest `hanamori-toolchain.json` in the current directory or its\nancestors wins. Nested projects override their parents. Outside a project, the default\ntoolchain is selected; without either a project or a default, the current environment stays\nunchanged. Invalid configuration, ambiguous matches and missing toolchains report errors\nwithout replacing the environment or downloading tools. An unchanged target produces no\nenvironment updates or repeated notices."],[1162,"On native ARM64, replace the build target, executable path and test target with\n`aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`. Version, size and SHA-256 come from the supplied executable.\nLocal HTTP fixtures serve releases and downloads; profiles and registry keys are isolated.\nPowerShell 5.1/7 cover first and repeated installation, Unicode paths, PATH preservation,\nskip options and retaining the old executable after download, digest, size or version failures.\nGit Bash and MSYS2 each cover piped installation, both path formats, repeat installation,\nfailure preservation, skip options and hook loading in a fresh Bash session."],[732,"On Windows the executable is `target/release/hanamori.exe`. No `aria2c`, `msiexec`, or\nVisual Studio installation is needed to run the installer. Building requires Rust and a linker for the chosen target; the Windows MSVC target needs the corresponding build tools.\nThe repository is licyk/Hanamori."],[1170,"On Windows x64 / ARM64 without Visual Studio/Build Tools, install A with `--vs-version 2022` and B with the default VS 2026, using different compiler/SDK versions and the default components (including MSBuild), set the same three environment variables, then run:"],[1111,"On Windows, a temporary PowerShell script waits for the parent process to exit, then deletes\nthe exact executable and backup paths. The CLI reports **scheduled**, not completed, removal;\nthe helper reports its result separately. It never kills other processes. If deletion fails,\nit retains `failure.txt`, `files.json` and `uninstall.ps1` in the displayed temporary directory.\nClose processes holding the files and rerun `uninstall.ps1` without arguments. Successful\ncleanup deletes the helper's own files and empty temporary directory."],[1123,"On Windows, Bash/Zsh hooks and profile loaders use the current MSYS runtime's `cygpath`\nto translate Hanamori's native executable path before invoking it. Keep `cygpath` on\nPATH. After upgrading from a build that embedded an unconverted Windows path, regenerate\nand apply `env`; if you installed a startup entry, rerun `shell init` with the executable\ndirectly to replace that loader as well."],[915,"On Windows, the default is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori`. Shell hooks, startup loaders and completion use this same selection rule; they do not save a separate manager binding. Set `HANAMORI_HOME` before loading the hook when you want a custom directory."],[1106,"On Windows, the installer records only the user PATH entry it added in the adjacent\n`hanamori.exe.install.json`. Self uninstall removes that entry and receipt, preserving\nother PATH entries and environment-variable references. Entries that existed before\ninstallation remain user-owned. Moving the executable requires manually cleaning the\noriginal installation's PATH entry."],[704,"One-command installation"],[862,"Open a new terminal or follow the printed profile reload instruction. The startup block stores a loader that generates completion from the executable on each startup, so new sessions use the updated command definitions after an upgrade. Normal `shell init` does not enable completion. Keep `--completions` when updating the managed block; omitting it switches the block back to loading only the hook."],[688,"Opening a VSIX identifies the compiler directory version, normalizes output paths and\ncounts files together. Extraction reuses this metadata and streams files directly into\nthe installation transaction's private staging tree. MSI file, directory, component and\nmedia mappings are prepared once for counting and extraction; discovering CAB downloads\nstill requires an earlier read of the MSI media table."],[1051,"Optional `x64` or `arm64`; host defaults to native Windows architecture, target defaults to host"],[1049,"Optional boolean: `true` requires MSBuild, `false` excludes it; omitted leaves local selection unconstrained; installation enables it by default with the SDK, or disables it when SDK is `null`"],[1053,"Optional source constraints; source-unknown imports cannot satisfy them"],[1055,"Optional, currently `1`"],[810,"Options"],[729,"Options are `--version`, `--install-dir`, `--no-path-update` and `--no-shell`. Installation directories accept MSYS or Windows paths. `--no-shell` skips Bash startup and completion setup; `--no-path-update` skips user PATH configuration."],[754,"Output conventions"],[1163,"Override installer runtimes with `HANAMORI_TEST_POWERSHELL`, `HANAMORI_TEST_PWSH` and\n`HANAMORI_TEST_BASH`. Bash also checks PATH, the Git installation found on PATH and the\ndefault Git installation. Additional MSYS2 uses `HANAMORI_TEST_MSYS2_BASH` or\n`msys64/usr/bin/bash.exe` on the system drive. Without `--require-shells`, unavailable\ndefault runtimes are reported as skipped; explicit missing runtimes always fail, as does\nan entirely skipped run. `--require-shells` requires all primary shells for the suite;\nadditional MSYS2 may still be skipped unless explicitly configured. Windows CI explicitly\nselects Git Bash; x64 also requires MSYS2, while ARM64 checks additional MSYS2 when available."],[714,"Parameter"],[790,"Parameters and result"],[684,"parent modules (`lib.rs` and any file with child modules) contain only `mod`\ndeclarations and re-exports, so implementation lives in leaf modules."],[1193,"Pass `--shell powershell/bash/zsh/cmd`; changing `$SHELL` or COMSPEC is not a fix"],[650,"Paths, locking, file usage handling, layout, versions and identity"],[696,"Persistent entries"],[1033,"Persistent startup profiles"],[1040,"Pin project requirements and understand local resolution."],[1183,"Place the Hanamori block after framework/compinit initialization, then reload it; the toolchain hook remains usable"],[1131,"Platform support"],[707,"Portable installation"],[1141,"POSIX shells on Windows"],[270,"PowerShell"],[403,"PowerShell"],[898,"PowerShell"],[1026,"PowerShell"],[1140,"PowerShell 5.1/7, Bash, Zsh; CMD is experimental"],[523,"PowerShell 5.1/7、Bash、Zsh；CMD 为实验性支持"],[1186,"PowerShell does not complete fixed values such as channel"],[573,"PowerShell 不补全 channel 等固定参数值"],[539,"PowerShell 中先设置 `$env:HANAMORI_REQUIRE_SHELL_TESTS = '1'`，再运行 Cargo。既有 CI 覆盖 Linux 与 Windows，测试使用真实实现、本地