sh runtime to configure `.bashrc`, login startup and completions. It defaults to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori\\bin`, installs no toolchains and leaves PowerShell profiles unchanged."],[962,"The child inherits stdin, stdout and stderr, and its exit status is returned to the caller. Only the child gets the prepared environment; the parent is not activated. Through a PowerShell hook, quote `'--'` to pass the separator. Windows PowerShell uses the encoded argv forwarding path to preserve empty strings and quotes."],[1147,"The CLI provides the `run` execution alias, the `completions` command and optional `--use-on-cd` project switching. There is currently no GUI, ARM32/ARM64EC target or cross-manager reference ledger. Loading a hook does not activate by default. Explicit `--auto-activate` attempts activation once in an inactive session; `--use-on-cd` also reselects on directory changes. See Shell integration for shell-specific triggers."],[1098,"The crates.io channel runs `cargo publish --locked`, retaining Cargo's compilation check of the packaged source. Only `hanamori` is published, not `hanamori-test-support` or `xtask`."],[1107,"The default removes the running executable, its `.outdated` upgrade backup, and recorded\nstartup entries belonging to that executable. MSVC, SDKs, configuration and named references\nremain available for a later installation of Hanamori. The executable's parent directory\nis never recursively deleted: a portable copy in Downloads does not give Hanamori ownership\nof Downloads."],[642,"The environment includes PATH, INCLUDE, LIB, `CC`/`CXX`, `VCToolsVersion`,\n`VCToolsInstallDir`, `VCINSTALLDIR`, `VSCMD_ARG_HOST_ARCH`, `VSCMD_ARG_TGT_ARCH`,\n`DISTUTILS_USE_SDK`, and SDK root/bin/version variables when applicable. POSIX shells get\nPOSIX executable paths; compiler-consumed INCLUDE/LIB paths retain Windows form. Hanamori\ndoes not generate `vcvarsall.bat` or `vcvars64.bat`."],[1070,"The example uses both the C++ standard library and Windows SDK. Do not install with `--no-sdk` for this example."],[1227,"The existing `--proxy`, `HANAMORI_PROXY` and configuration `proxy` setting apply to both\nthe API query and download. Optional `GITHUB_TOKEN` authenticates only the API request;\nit is not sent to the asset download. Toolchain mirrors, caches, download directories\nand project files do not control self-update. Other platforms/build targets currently\nhave no self-update asset."],[1171,"The gate selects v143/v145 for each toolchain and builds `.vcxproj` and `.sln` files referencing a static-library project in A → B (inheriting A) → A order. It exercises Debug/Release, resources, manifests, incremental compilation, changed-library relinking, Clean/Rebuild and evaluated compiler/SDK/targets paths inside the selected installation. An explicitly unavailable SDK must fail. Builds disable node reuse; binary logs reside in the temporary build directory."],[1097,"The GitHub channel builds on Windows x64 and `windows-11-arm`, packaging `hanamori-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe`, `hanamori-aarch64-pc-windows-msvc.exe` and matching ZIPs containing `hanamori.exe`. All four published asset SHA-256 digests are verified."],[1001,"The host needs the .NET Framework required by MSBuild. Installation extracts and checks files; on Windows, `doctor` also runs `MSBuild.exe -version` and reports runtime failures without installing system components. Invoke `MSBuild.exe` through the Hanamori environment so generated configuration selects the local compiler and SDK. Explicit conflicting project versions fail the build."],[1235,"The independent `site/` project adapts RVC Next’s Fumadocs/TanStack Start framework. It uses React, Tailwind, MDX, Bun and Vitest. Provenance and licensing are in `site/NOTICE` and `site/LICENSE`."],[738,"The installer chooses the native Windows architecture, including when launched from an emulated shell. Override with PowerShell `-Architecture x64` / `-Architecture arm64`, or Bash `--architecture x64` / `--architecture arm64`. This selects Hanamori itself; `hanamori install --arch HOST/TARGET` selects the compiler independently."],[683,"the layer directions in the table;"],[914,"The manager directory is chosen by `--manager-dir`, then `HANAMORI_HOME`, then the platform\nlocal-data directory under `Hanamori`. Read `<manager>/config.json` after choosing it:"],[1243,"The pinned static Server Function middleware requests its cache from the root path. A build transform in `vite.config.ts` prefixes client requests with the base path while keeping cache files at the output root. Recheck documentation navigation under a subpath when upgrading this dependency."],[713,"The priority is `-InstallDir`, then `HANAMORI_INSTALL_DIR`, then `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori\\bin`. An unset or empty environment variable uses the default directory."],[963,"The public command is `exec`; there is no `run` alias. This differs from activating the current shell."],[733,"The release workflow produces\nEXE and ZIP assets for `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` and `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc`, named\n`hanamori-<target>.exe` and `hanamori-<target>.zip`. The ZIP entry is `hanamori.exe`."],[1080,"The Release workflow publishes both GitHub Release assets and the `hanamori` crate. Pushing a `v*` tag publishes to both channels. Manual runs let you choose a tag and a channel. Ordinary main pushes and website builds do not publish versions."],[1095,"The reusable CI workflow and Installers workflow check Rust code and installer scripts separately at the same commit. Rust checks include formatting, module architecture and tests; installer checks cover arguments and metadata on Linux and native installation on Windows. Windows uses the release profile and `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` / `aarch64-pc-windows-msvc` target."],[710,"The script downloads the latest stable release, checks its SHA-256, size and reported version, and installs `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Hanamori\\bin\\hanamori.exe`. It adds the directory to your user PATH and initializes the current PowerShell profile and session with completions. It requires no administrator privileges and downloads no toolchains. Running inline takes effect immediately; running in a child process requires opening a new terminal afterward."],[950,"The SDK tool path is `Windows Kits/10/bin/<version>/<host>`, so activation and `exec` make `rc.exe` and `mt.exe` available by name. `WindowsSdkVerBinPath` still points to the version directory without the architecture. Installation checks include both tools and their bundled DLLs; rerun the corresponding `install` command to repair missing files in a managed installation."],[1245,"The site workflow validates builds for pull requests. Website changes on main or a manual run on main also force-push `.output/public` to the `gh-pages` branch after validation, using the repository secret `GITEE_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY`. The key needs repository write access. In the repository Pages settings, select `Deploy from a branch`, the `gh-pages` branch, and `/ (root)`. Netlify, Cloudflare Pages and Vercel configuration uses the same `.output/public` output and requires separate platform setup."],[999,"The supported scope is native C++ `.vcxproj` and `.sln` builds using VS 2026 v145 or VS 2022 v143. Use `--vs-version 2022` for v143 projects. Win32, ATL/MFC, C++/CLI, UWP, drivers, C# and IDE integration are outside that scope. Native Windows build acceptance remains pending; real downloads/extraction and Linux tests do not establish it."],[692,"The target lock protects preparation in a sibling `.<name>.stage` directory on the destination volume. Publication renames the old tree to `.old`, moves the new tree into place, then removes the old tree. Failed preparation preserves existing files. The next install cleans interrupted staging and restores `.old` when the final directory is missing; ordinary reuse also runs this cleanup. Missing managed directories or required files trigger installation. Use `--reinstall` for damage beyond the quick required-file checks."],[1099,"The two channels run independently after shared checks pass. If one fails, retry only the unpublished channel with the same tag. When manually publishing an older tag, checks and builds use that tag's source, not the main source that defines the workflow."],[1242,"The Umami analytics script and website ID are configured in `src/routes/__root.tsx`. Documentation comments use the `Comment` category in Hanamori’s GitHub Discussions, configured in `src/lib/giscus.ts`. Giscus maps discussions by pathname, uses Chinese (`zh-CN`), and follows the system color scheme. No comment-related environment variables are required."],[681,"The unpublished `test-support` crate holds synthetic payloads, HTTP fixtures and shell\nprobes for tests. `cargo xtask check` enforces the structure and runs in CI:"],[1226,"The updater downloads the EXE matching the running executable architecture directly. The Release asset\nmust supply a SHA-256 digest; its hash and size must match, and the candidate must\nsuccessfully report the expected `hanamori --version` within ten seconds. Missing or\ninvalid metadata, download errors and failed verification leave the current executable\nin place. The next invocation after a successful update uses the new version."],[1161,"The Windows suite accepts a real built EXE; the test runner never invokes Cargo itself.\nFor a native x64 host:"],[1092,"The workflow does not create tags. Publication stops if there is no `v*` tag, the requested tag does not exist, or the tag version differs from the Cargo version in its source. A tag push selects that tag; an explicit manual `tag` input takes precedence."],[972,"There are three distinct identifiers:"],[867,"These commands load both the `use/deactivate` hook and completion. To load completion alone, replace `env --completions` with `completions`; it neither installs an environment hook nor activates a toolchain."],[1175,"This gate compiles and links C/C++ with the actual compiler and builds a `.vcxproj` with MSBuild. It checks PE Machine (`0x8664` or `0xaa64`) and executes the result when the OS supports its target. Run x64/arm64 on x64 Windows; run arm64/arm64, arm64/x64 and x64/arm64 on Windows 11 ARM64. The two-toolchain gates also accept ARM64 installations and use their selected MSBuild platform. Real Windows acceptance remains separate from Linux extraction checks."],[1168,"This ignored gate runs in the sequence A → B (inheriting A) → A from an isolated environment.\nIt invokes `rc.exe` by name to compile resources, compiles and links C++ using Windows/standard\nheaders, the static CRT and SDK libraries, then invokes `mt.exe` by name to embed a manifest.\nThe built program checks the resource and embedded manifest contents. The gate also checks\ndistinct/stable compiler fingerprints and unchanged reference contents, using paths with spaces and Unicode.\nIt downloads or deletes no tools. Missing inputs or a non-Windows host fail explicitly.\nCross-compilation, Linux synthetic tests and Wine do not establish native acceptance.\nInteractive PowerShell 5.1/7, Git Bash/Zsh, CMD/AutoRun, independent terminals, cross-volume\noperations and preservation when files are occupied must each be verified with their results recorded."],[755,"This page follows the current Clap definitions. See individual guides for environment and directory semantics. `hanamori --help` and `hanamori COMMAND --help` describe the installed build. There is no `run` alias."],[1073,"This removes the whole managed installation and its aliases, not `hello.cpp` in your project. Do not store personal files inside toolchain directories. To delete only the stable name, use `remove stable`; the managed directory remains discoverable by list. See maintenance."],[1032,"Through the wrapper, write the `exec` separator as `'--'`. Inspect `$LASTEXITCODE` for native child status. `shell deinit` affects future loads; restart the terminal to discard the already loaded function."],[711,"To choose a release or executable directory:"],[1105,"To uninstall Hanamori itself:"],[977,"toolset `14.44.17.14`, SDK `26100`"],[352,"toolset `14.44.17.14`，SDK `26100`"],[1176,"Troubleshooting"],[628,"Umami 统计脚本及网站 ID 配置位于 `src/routes/__root.tsx`。文档评论使用 Hanamori GitHub Discussions 的 `Comment` 分类，配置位于 `src/lib/giscus.ts`。Giscus 按 pathname 关联讨论，使用中文（`zh-CN`）界面，并跟随系统配色，无需额外设置评论相关环境变量。"],[970,"Understand download IDs, actual versions and independent installations."],[948,"Understand managed variables, switching and restoration boundaries."],[1020,"Uninstall accepts a directory key, reference or unique version prefix. Missing payload files do not prevent removal. If the entire directory is gone, its exact key or dangling managed reference still allows cleanup. Deactivate a toolchain used by the current session first. On Windows, after acquiring the directory lock, uninstall uses Windows Restart Manager to close processes using the target files before deleting the directory. Toolchain cleanup during `self uninstall --purge` follows the same flow."],[1103,"Uninstall Hanamori"],[916,"Unknown fields are ignored; optional `schema_version` is currently `1`. Other values use\nexplicit CLI > nonempty environment variable > configuration file > default. Manager\nlocation is not read back from its own configuration file."],[1056,"Unknown fields are ignored. The nearest file in the current directory or its ancestors\nwins. A malformed nearest file stops selection rather than falling through to a parent\nor the default. Selection priority is explicit selector/directory, then project, then\n`default`. Missing matches fail; several matches list candidates and require a directory key or\nalias. A numeric prefix does not silently pick one SDK or source over another."],[1223,"Update a Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC build from a verified GitHub Release."],[1216,"Update asset/digest missing"],[1211,"Update the reference with `import --dir NEW --name NAME`"],[1093,"Update the workspace version and Cargo-generated lockfile, then create a `v*` tag pointing to the intended source."],[1228,"Updating requires write access to the executable's directory. Staging is created beside\nthat executable, and a sibling `<executable>.update.lock` prevents simultaneous updates.\nThe lock file may remain after completion; do not delete it to bypass an active update.\nThe old executable is renamed to `<executable>.outdated`, retained while its process\nexits, and removed by the next actual update. After verifying the new executable, if backup\ndeletion is blocked by file usage, Windows Restart Manager closes its users and retries.\nResolve any remaining error manually. These sibling names are reserved for the updater."],[880,"Usable managed directory keys, managed references and unambiguous versions"],[734,"Use the download page to choose a release for your architecture. Rename the standalone EXE to `hanamori.exe`, or extract it from the ZIP, and place it in a tools directory such as `D:\\Tools\\Hanamori`. No Rust installation is needed to run a downloaded executable."],[1081,"Use the repository's `xtask` commands from the workspace or one of its packages:"],[129,"VERSION 为托管目录键、实际版本/前缀或 latest；无显式约束时选择渠道最新，项目可提供约束"],[57,"VSIX 打开时统一识别编译器目录版本、规范化输出路径并统计文件，解包复用这些元数据，直接流式写入安装事务的私有暂存树。MSI 的文件、目录、组件和介质映射也在准备阶段解析一次，供计数和解包共用；下载 CAB 前仍需先读取 MSI 的介质表。"],[654,"VSIX, MSI and CAB extraction"],[22,"VSIX、MSI、CAB 解包"],[1231,"Website maintenance"],[886,"When multiple installations share an MSVC version, for example with different SDKs, that version cannot select an installation uniquely. Completion offers exact directory keys and references instead. Activation candidates exclude unusable directories; remove/unalias can still suggest dangling references. Completion changes no files and does not replace execution-time checks."],[695,"Windows paths"],[524,"Windows POSIX Shell"],[1218,"Windows self removal failed"],[1136,"Windows x64 / ARM64 hosts; x64 and ARM64 targets"],[1224,"Windows x64 / ARM64 MSVC builds can 